<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<usx version="2.6">
  <book code="2SA" style="id">- Tov Rose New Messianic Version Bible</book>
  <para style="h">2 Samuel</para>
  <para style="mt">2 Samuel</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now it came to pass after the death of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, when David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> was returned from the slaughter of the ‘Amalekim <char style="add">[Dwellers in a Valley]</char>, and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> had abode two days in Ziklag <char style="add">[Winding]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />It came even to pass on the third day, that, behold, a man came out of the camp from Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> with his clothes rent, and earth upon his head: and <char style="add">[so]</char> it was, when he came to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, that he fell to the earth, and did obesiance <char style="pn">(bowing or kneeling in respect)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto him, From where do you<char style="ord">i</char> come? And he said unto him, Out of the camp of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> am I escaped.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto him, How went the matter? I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, tell me. And he answered, That the people are fled from the battle, and many of the people also are fallen and dead; and Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> his son are dead also.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto the young man that told him, How know you<char style="ord">i</char> that Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> his son be dead?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the young man that told him said, As I happened by chance upon mount Gilboa <char style="add">[swollen heap]</char>, behold, Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> leaned upon his spear; and, lo, the chariots and horsemen followed hard after him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And when he looked behind him, he saw me, and called unto me. And I answered, Here <char style="add">[am]</char> I.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And he said unto me, Who <char style="add">[are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>? And I answered him, I <char style="add">[am]</char> an ‘Amaleki <char style="add">[Dwellers in a Valley]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />He said unto me again, Stand, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, upon me, and slay me: for anguish is come upon me, because my life <char style="add">[is]</char> yet whole in me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />So I stood upon him, and killed him, because I was sure that he could not live after that he was fallen: and I took the crown that <char style="add">[was]</char> upon his head, and the bracelet that <char style="add">[was]</char> on his arm, and have brought them here unto my lord.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Then David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> took hold on his clothes, and rent them; and likewise all the men that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And they mourned, and wept, and fasted until even, for Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, and for Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> his son, and for the people of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and for the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; because they were fallen by the sword.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto the young man that told him, Whence <char style="add">[are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>? And he answered, I <char style="add">[am]</char> the son of a stranger, an ‘Amaleki <char style="add">[Dwellers in a Valley]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto him, How were you<char style="ord">i</char> not afraid to stretch forth you<char style="ord">i</char> hand to destroy the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> anointed?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> called one of the young men, and said, Go near, <char style="add">[and]</char> fall upon him. And he struck him that he died.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto him, You<char style="ord">1s</char> blood <char style="add">[be]</char> upon you<char style="ord">i</char> head; for you<char style="ord">i</char> mouth has testified against you<char style="ord">i</char>, saying, I have slain the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> anointed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> lamented with this lamentation over Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and over Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> his son:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />(Also he bade them teach the children of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised] [the use of]</char> the bow: behold, <char style="add">[it is]</char> written in the book of Yahsar <char style="add">[Upright, Correct]</char>.)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />The beauty of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> is slain upon you<char style="ord">i</char> high places: how are the mighty fallen!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Tell <char style="add">[it]</char> not in Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char>, publish <char style="add">[it]</char> not in the streets of Askelon [The Fire of Infamy: I shall be Weighed]; lest the daughters of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> rejoice, lest the daughters of the uncircumcised triumph.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> mountains of Gilboa <char style="add">[swollen heap]</char>, <char style="add">[let there be]</char> no dew, neither <char style="add">[let there be]</char> rain, upon you, nor fields of offerings: for there the shield of the mighty is vilely cast away, the shield of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, <char style="add">[as though he had]</char> not <char style="add">[been]</char> anointed with oil.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />From the blood of the slain, from the fat of the mighty, the bow of Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> turned not back, and the sword of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> returned not empty.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given] [were]</char> lovely and pleasant in their lives, and in their death they were not divided: they were swifter than eagles, they were stronger than lions.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> daughters of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, weep over Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, who clothed you in scarlet, with <char style="add">[other]</char> delights, who put on ornaments of gold upon your apparel.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />How are the mighty fallen in the midst of the battle! O Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>, <char style="add">[you<char style="ord">i</char> were]</char> slain in you<char style="ord">i</char> high places.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />I am distressed for you<char style="ord">i</char>, my brother Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>: very pleasant have you<char style="ord">i</char> been unto me: you<char style="ord">i</char> love to me was wonderful, passing the love of women.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />How are the mighty fallen, and the weapons of war perished!</para>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass after this, that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> enquired of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, saying, Shall I go up into any of the cities of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>? And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto him, Go up. And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said, Where shall I go up? And he said, Unto Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />So David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> went up there, and his two wives also, Achino’am <char style="add">[my brother is delight]</char> the Yizre’elit <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>, and Avigayil <char style="add">[my father is joy]</char> Naval <char style="add">[fool]</char>’s wife the Carmeli <char style="add">[garden-land]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And his men that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him did David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> bring up, every man with his household: and they dwelt in the cities of Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the men of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> came, and there they anointed David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> king over the house of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>. And they told David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, saying, <char style="add">[That]</char> the men of Yavesh-Gil’ad <char style="add">[Dry Hill of Testimony] [were they]</char> that buried Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> sent messengers unto the men of Yavesh-Gil’ad <char style="add">[Dry Hill of Testimony]</char>, and said unto them, Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> you<char style="ord">2f</char> of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> have showed this kindness unto your lord, <char style="add">[even]</char> unto Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, and have buried him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And now the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> show kindness and tunto you: and I also will requite <char style="pn">(repay)</char> you this kindness, because you<char style="ord">2f</char> have done this thing.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Therefore now let your hands be strengthened, and be you<char style="ord">2f</char> valiant: for your master Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> is dead, and also the house of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> have anointed me king over them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />But Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> the son of Ner <char style="add">[lamp]</char>, captain of Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> host, took Ish-Boshet <char style="add">[man of shame]</char> the son of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, and brought him over to Machanayim <char style="add">[Two Camps]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And made him king over Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>, and over the Ashuri <char style="add">[guided; Blessed (Favored by God; happy; prosperous)],</char> and over Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>, and over Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, and over Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, and over all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Ish-Boshet <char style="add">[man of shame]</char> Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> son <char style="add">[was]</char> forty years old when he began to reign over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and reigned two years. But the house of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> followed David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the time that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> was king in Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char> over the house of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> was seven years and six months.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> the son of Ner <char style="add">[lamp]</char>, and the servants of Ish-Boshet <char style="add">[man of shame]</char> the son of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, went out from Machanayim <char style="add">[Two Camps]</char> to Giv’on <char style="add">[Hill City]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> the son of Tz’ruyah <char style="add">[balsam]</char>, and the servants of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, went out, and met together by the pool of Giv’on <char style="add">[Hill City]</char>: and they sat down, the one on the one side of the pool, and the other on the other side of the pool.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> said to Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, Let the young men now arise, and play before us. And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> said, Let them arise.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Then there arose and went over by number twelve of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, which <char style="add">[pertained]</char> to Ish-Boshet <char style="add">[man of shame]</char> the son of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, and twelve of the servants of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And they caught everyone his fellow by the head, and <char style="add">[thrust]</char> his sword in his fellow’s side; so they fell down together: wherefore that place was called Helkat-Hatzurim <char style="add">[field of swords]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> in Giv’on <char style="add">[Hill City]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And there was a very sore battle that day; and Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> was beaten, and the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, before the servants of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And there were three sons of Tz’ruyah <char style="add">[balsam]</char> there, Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, and Avishai <char style="add">[my father is a gift]</char>, and ‘Asah’el <char style="add">[God-made]</char>: and ‘Asah’el <char style="add">[God-made] [was as]</char> light of foot as a wild roe.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And ‘Asah’el <char style="add">[God-made]</char> pursued after Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char>; and in going he turned not to the right hand nor to the left from following Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Then Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> looked behind him, and said, <char style="add">[Are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> ‘Asah’el <char style="add">[God-made]</char>? And he answered, I <char style="add">[am]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> said to him, Turn you<char style="ord">i</char> aside to you<char style="ord">i</char> right hand or to you<char style="ord">i</char> left, and lay you<char style="ord">i</char> hold on one of the young men, and take you<char style="ord">i</char> his armour. But ‘Asah’el <char style="add">[God-made]</char> would not turn aside from following of him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> said again to ‘Asah’el <char style="add">[God-made]</char>, Turn you<char style="ord">i</char> aside from following me: wherefore should I strike you<char style="ord">i</char> to the ground? how then should I hold up my face to Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> brother?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />However he refused to turn aside: wherefore Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> with the behind <char style="pn">(the back side; the rear)</char> of the spear struck him under the fifth <char style="add">[rib]</char>, that the spear came out behind him; and he fell down there, and died in the same place: and it came to pass, <char style="add">[that]</char> as many as came to the place where ‘Asah’el <char style="add">[God-made]</char> fell down and died stood still.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> also and Avishai <char style="add">[my father is a gift]</char> pursued after Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char>: and the sun went down when they were come to the hill of Amah <char style="add">[a cubit]</char>, that <char style="add">[lies]</char> before Giach <char style="add">[to break forth]</char> by the way of the wilderness of Giv’on <char style="add">[Hill City]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And the children of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> gathered themselves together after Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char>, and became one troop, and stood on the top of an hill.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Then Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> called to Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, and said, Shall the sword devour forever? know you<char style="ord">i</char> not that it will be bitterness in the latter end? how long shall it be then, before you<char style="ord">i</char> bid the people return from following their brethren?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> said, <char style="add">[As]</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> lives, unless you<char style="ord">i</char> had spoken, surely then in the morning the people had gone up everyone from following his brother.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />So Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> blew a trumpet, and all the people stood still, and pursued after Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> no more, neither fought they any more.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> and his men walked all that night through the plain, and passed over Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>, and went through all Bitron [division, or cleft <char style="pn">(split hoof; an opening, break or split)</char>, or ravine], and they came to Machanayim <char style="add">[Two Camps]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> returned from following Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char>: and when he had gathered all the people together, there lacked of David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s servants nineteen men and ‘Asah’el <char style="add">[God-made]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />But the servants of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> had smitten of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, and of Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char>’s men, <char style="add">[so that]</char> three hundred and threescore men died.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And they took up ‘Asah’el <char style="add">[God-made]</char>, and buried him in the sepulcher of his father, which <char style="add">[was in]</char> Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char>. And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> and his men went all night, and they came to Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char> at break of day.</para>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now there was long war between the house of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and the house of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>: but David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> waxed stronger and stronger, and the house of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> waxed weaker and weaker.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> were sons born in Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char>: and his firstborn was Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char>, of Achino’am <char style="add">[my brother is delight]</char> the Yizre’elit <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And his second, Kil’av <char style="add">[like his father]</char>, of Avigayil <char style="add">[my father is joy]</char> the wife of Naval <char style="add">[fool]</char> the Carmeli <char style="add">[garden-land]</char>; and the third, Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> the son of Ma’akhah <char style="add">[oppression] [oppression]</char> the daughter of Talmai <char style="add">[Plowman]</char> king of G’shur <char style="add">[proud beholder]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the fourth, Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char> the son of Haggit <char style="add">[festive]</char>; and the fifth, Sh’fatyah <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> the son of Avital <char style="add">[my father is (the) dew]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the sixth, Yitre’am <char style="add">[profit of the people]</char>, by ‘Eglah <char style="add">[a heifer]</char> David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s wife. These were born to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> in Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And it came to pass, while there was war between the house of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and the house of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, that Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> made himself strong for the house of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> had a concubine, whose name <char style="add">[was]</char> Ritzpah <char style="add">[pavement]</char>, the daughter of Ayah <char style="add">[falcon]</char>: and [Ish-Boshet <char style="add">[man of shame]</char>] said to Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char>, For what reason have you<char style="ord">i</char> gone in unto my father’s concubine?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Then was Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> very exceedingly angry for the words of Ish-Boshet <char style="add">[man of shame]</char>, and said, <char style="add">[Am]</char> I a dog’s head, which against Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> do show kindness this day unto the house of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> father, to his brethren, and to his friends, and have not delivered you<char style="ord">i</char> into the hand of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, that you<char style="ord">i</char> charge me to day with a fault concerning this woman?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />So do God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> to Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char>, and more also, except, as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has sworn to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, even so I do to him;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />To translate <char style="pn">(transfer; remove to another place)</char> the kingdom from the house of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, and to set up the throne of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and over Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, from Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char> even to Be’er-sheva <char style="add">[Well of the sevenfold Oath]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And he could not answer Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> a word again, because he feared him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> sent messengers to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> on his behalf, saying, Whose <char style="add">[is]</char> the land? saying <char style="add">[also]</char>, Make your<char style="ord">i</char> league with me, and, behold, my hand <char style="add">[shall be]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char>, to bring about all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> unto you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And he said, Well; I will make a league with you<char style="ord">i</char>: but one thing I require of you<char style="ord">i</char>, that is, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not see my face, except you<char style="ord">i</char> first bring Mikhal <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> daughter, when you<char style="ord">i</char> come to see my face.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> sent messengers to Ish-Boshet <char style="add">[man of shame]</char> Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> son, saying, Deliver <char style="add">[me]</char> my wife Mikhal <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char>, which I espoused to me for an hundred foreskins of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Ish-Boshet <char style="add">[man of shame]</char> sent, and took her from <char style="add">[her]</char> husband, <char style="add">[even]</char> from Palti’el <char style="add">[God delivers]</char> the son of Layish <char style="add">[Lion]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And her husband went with her along weeping behind her to Bachurim <char style="add">[young men’s Villiage]</char>. Then said Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> unto him, Go, return. And he returned.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> had communication with the elders of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, saying, You<char style="ord">2f</char> sought for David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> in times past <char style="add">[to be]</char> king over you:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Now then do <char style="add">[it]</char>: for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has spoken of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, saying, By the hand of my servant David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> I will save my people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> out of the hand of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and out of the hand of all their enemies.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> also spoke in the ears of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>: and Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> went also to speak in the ears of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> in Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char> all that seemed good to Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and that seemed good to the whole house of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />So Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> came to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> to Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char>, and twenty men with him. And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> made Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> and the men that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him a feast.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> said unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, I will arise and go, and will gather all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> unto my lord the king, that they may make a league with you<char style="ord">i</char>, and that you<char style="ord">i</char> may reign over all that you<char style="ord">i</char> heart desires. And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> sent Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> away; and he went in peace.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And, behold, the servants of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> came from <char style="add">[pursuing]</char> a troop, and brought in a great spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> with them: but Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp] [was]</char> not with David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> in Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char>; for he had sent him away, and he was gone in peace.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />When Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> and all the host that <char style="add">[was]</char> with him were come, they told Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, saying, Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> the son of Ner <char style="add">[lamp]</char> came to the king, and he has sent him away, and he is gone in peace.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Then Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> came to the king, and said, What have you<char style="ord">i</char> done? behold, Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> came unto you<char style="ord">i</char>; why <char style="add">[is]</char> it <char style="add">[that]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> have sent him away, and he is quite gone?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> know Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> the son of Ner <char style="add">[lamp]</char>, that he came to deceive you<char style="ord">i</char>, and to know your<char style="ord">i</char> going out and your<char style="ord">i</char> coming in, and to know all that you<char style="ord">i</char> do.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And when Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> was come out from David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, he sent messengers after Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char>, which brought him again from the well of Sirah <char style="add">[the turning]</char>: but David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> knew <char style="add">[it]</char> not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And when Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> was returned to Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char>, Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> took him aside in the gate to speak with him quietly, and struck him there under the fifth <char style="add">[rib]</char>, that he died, for the blood of ‘Asah’el <char style="add">[God-made]</char> his brother.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And afterward when David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> heard <char style="add">[it]</char>, he said, I and my kingdom <char style="add">[are]</char> guiltless before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> forever from the blood of Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> the son of Ner <char style="add">[lamp]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />Let it rest on the head of Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, and on all his father’s house; and let there not fail from the house of Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> one that has an issue <char style="pn">(what comes forth)</char>, or that is a leper, or that leans on a staff, or that falls on the sword, or that lacks bread.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />So Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> and Avishai <char style="add">[my father is a gift]</char> his brother killed Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char>, because he had slain their brother ‘Asah’el <char style="add">[God-made]</char> at Giv’on <char style="add">[Hill City]</char> in the battle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said to Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, and to all the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him, Rend <char style="pn">(tear apart; forcefully rip apart)</char> your clothes, and gird you with sackcloth, and mourn before Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char>. And king David <char style="add">[beloved] [himself]</char> followed the bier.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And they buried Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> in Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char>: and the king lifted up his voice, and wept at the grave of Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char>; and all the people wept.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And the king lamented over Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char>, and said, Died Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> as a fool dies?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />Your<char style="ord">1s</char> hands <char style="add">[were]</char> not bound, nor your<char style="ord">i</char> feet put into fetters: as a man falls before wicked men, <char style="add">[so]</char> fell you<char style="ord">i</char>. And all the people wept again over him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And when all the people came to cause David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> to eat meat while it was yet day, David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> swore, saying, So do God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> to me, and more also, if I taste bread, or ought else, till the sun be down.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And all the people took notice <char style="add">[of it]</char>, and it pleased them: as whatsoever the king did pleased all the people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />For all the people and all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> understood that day that it was not of the king to slay Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> the son of Ner <char style="add">[lamp]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And the king said unto his servants, Know you<char style="ord">2f</char> not that there is a prince and a great man fallen this day in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />And I <char style="add">[am]</char> this day weak, though anointed king; and these men the sons of Tz’ruyah <char style="add">[balsam] [be]</char> too hard for me: the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall reward the doer of evil according to his wickedness.</para>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And when Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> son heard that Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> was dead in Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char>, his hands were feeble, and all the Yisra’eli’s were troubled.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> son had two men <char style="add">[that were]</char> captains of bands: the name of the one <char style="add">[was]</char> Ba’anah <char style="add">[in affliction]</char>, and the name of the other Rekhav <char style="add">[rider]</char>, the sons of Rimmon <char style="add">[Pomegranate]</char> a Be’erot <char style="add">[wells]</char>, of the children of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> (for B’erot <char style="add">[Wells]</char> also was reckoned to Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the Be’erotim <char style="add">[wells]</char> fled to Gittayim <char style="add">[two winepresses]</char>, and were sojourners there until this day.)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>, Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> son, had a son <char style="add">[that was]</char> lame of <char style="add">[his]</char> feet. He was five years old when the tidings came of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> out of Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>, and his nurse took him up, and fled: and it came to pass, as she made haste to flee, that he fell, and became lame. And his name <char style="add">[was]</char> M’fivoshet <char style="add">[exterminating the idol]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the sons of Rimmon <char style="add">[Pomegranate]</char> the Be’erot <char style="add">[wells]</char>, Rekhav <char style="add">[rider]</char> and Ba’anah <char style="add">[in affliction]</char>, went, and came about the heat of the day to the house of Ish-Boshet <char style="add">[man of shame]</char>, who lay on a bed at noon.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And they came there into the midst of the house, <char style="add">[as though]</char> they would have fetched wheat; and they struck him under the fifth <char style="add">[rib]</char>: and Rekhav <char style="add">[rider]</char> and Ba’anah <char style="add">[in affliction]</char> his brother escaped.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />For when they came into the house, he lay on his bed in his bedchamber, and they struck him, and killed him, and beheaded him, and took his head, and got them away through the plain all night.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And they brought the head of Ish-Boshet <char style="add">[man of shame]</char> unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> to Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char>, and said to the king, Behold the head of Ish-Boshet <char style="add">[man of shame]</char> the son of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> enemy, which sought you<char style="ord">i</char> life; and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has avenged my lord the king this day of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, and of his seed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> answered Rekhav <char style="add">[rider]</char> and Ba’anah <char style="add">[in affliction]</char> his brother, the sons of Rimmon <char style="add">[Pomegranate]</char> the Be’erot <char style="add">[wells]</char>, and said unto them, <char style="add">[As]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives, who has redeemed my soul out of all adversity,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />When one told me, saying, Behold, Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> is dead, thinking to have brought good tidings, I took hold of him, and killed him in Ziklag <char style="add">[Winding]</char>, who <char style="add">[thought]</char> that I would have given him a reward for his tidings:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />How much more, when wicked men have slain a righteous person in his own house upon his bed? shall I not therefore now require his blood of your hand, and take you away from the earth?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> commanded his young men, and they killed them, and cut off their hands and their feet, and hanged <char style="add">[them]</char> up over the pool in Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char>. But they took the head of Ish-Boshet <char style="add">[man of shame]</char>, and buried <char style="add">[it]</char> in the sepulcher of Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> in Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="5" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then came all the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> unto Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char>, and spoke, saying, Behold, we <char style="add">[are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> bone and you<char style="ord">i</char> flesh.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Also in time past, when Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> was king over us, you<char style="ord">i</char> were he that led out and brought in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said to you<char style="ord">i</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall feed my people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be a captain over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />So all the elders of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> came to the king to Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char>; and king David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> made a league with them in Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char> before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and they anointed David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> king over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />David <char style="add">[beloved] [was]</char> thirty years old when he began to reign, <char style="add">[and]</char> he reigned forty years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />In Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char> he reigned over Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> seven years and six months: and in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> he reigned thirty and three years over all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the king and his men went to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> unto the Y’vusi <char style="add">[Threshers, Trampled Under Foot]</char>, the inhabitants of the land: which spoke unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, saying, Except you<char style="ord">i</char> take away the blind and the lame, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not come in here: thinking, David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> cannot come in here.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Nevertheless David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> took the strong hold of Tziyon <char style="add">[parched place]</char>: the same <char style="add">[is]</char> the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said on that day, Whosoever gets up to the gutter, and smites the Y’vusi <char style="add">[Threshers, Trampled Under Foot]</char>, and the lame and the blind, <char style="add">[that are]</char> hated of David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s soul, <char style="add">[he shall be chief and captain]</char>. For what reason they said, The blind and the lame shall not come into the house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />So David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> dwelt in the fort, and called it the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>. And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> built round about from Millo <char style="add">[fortification (defensive structure) or mound]</char> and inward.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> went on, and grew great, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies] [was]</char> with him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And Hiram <char style="add">[noble]</char> king of Tzor <char style="pn">(Tyre)</char> <char style="add">[a rock]</char> sent messengers to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and cedar trees, and carpenters, and masons: and they built David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> an house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> perceived that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had established him king over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and that he had exalted his kingdom for his people Yisra’el’s <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> sake.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> took <char style="add">[him]</char> more concubines and wives out of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, after he was come from Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char>: and there were yet sons and daughters born to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And these <char style="add">[be]</char> the names of those that were born unto him in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>; Shamua <char style="add">[Renowned]</char>, and Shovav <char style="add">[rebellious]</char>, and Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char>, and Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Yivchar <char style="add">[Yehovah chooses]</char> also, and Elishua <char style="add">[my God is wealth]</char>, and Nefeg <char style="add">[Weak, Slacked]</char>, and Yafia <char style="add">[Shining]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And Elishama <char style="add">[My God has Heard]</char>, and El-yada <char style="add">[God knows]</char>, and Elifelet <char style="add">[God is deliverance]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />But when the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> heard that they had anointed David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> king over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, all the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> came up to seek David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>; and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> heard <char style="add">[of it]</char>, and went down to the hold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />The P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> also came and spread themselves in the valley of Refa’im <char style="add">[giants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> enquired of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, saying, Shall I go up to the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>? will you<char style="ord">i</char> deliver them into my hand? And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, Go up: for I will doubtless deliver the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> into you<char style="ord">i</char> hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> came to Ba’al-P’ratzim <char style="add">[lord of the breaks]</char>, and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> struck them there, and said, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has broken forth upon my enemies before me, as the breach <char style="pn">(breaking forth; a break; opening, inlet)</char> of waters. Therefore he called the name of that place Ba’al-P’ratzim <char style="add">[lord of the breaks]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And there they left their images, and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and his men burned them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> came up yet again, and spread themselves in the valley of Refa’im <char style="add">[giants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And when David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> enquired of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, he said, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not go up; <char style="add">[but]</char> fetch a compass <char style="pn">(go around, encircle; encompass)</char> behind them, and come upon them over against the mulberry trees.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And let it be, when you<char style="ord">i</char> hear the sound of a going in the tops of the mulberry trees, that then you<char style="ord">i</char> shall bestir yourself: for then shall the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> go out before you<char style="ord">i</char>, to strike the host of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> did so, as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had commanded him; and struck the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> from Geva <char style="add">[hill]</char> until you<char style="ord">i</char> come to Gezer <char style="add">[portion]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="6" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Again, David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> gathered together all <char style="add">[the]</char> chosen <char style="add">[men]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, thirty thousand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> arose, and went with all the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him from Ba’alei <char style="add">[the lords]</char> of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, to bring up from there the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, whose name is called by the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char> that dwells <char style="add">[between]</char> the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And they set the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> upon a new cart, and brought it out of the house of Avinadav <char style="add">[my father is noble]</char> that <char style="add">[was]</char> in Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>: and ‘Uzah <char style="add">[strength]</char> and Achyo <char style="add">[brotherly or fraternal]</char>, the sons of Avinadav <char style="add">[my father is noble]</char>, drove the new cart.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And they brought it out of the house of Avinadav <char style="add">[my father is noble]</char> which <char style="add">[was]</char> at Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>, accompanying the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>: and Achyo <char style="add">[brotherly or fraternal]</char> went before the ark.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and all the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> played before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> on all manner of <char style="add">[instruments made of]</char> fir wood, even on harps, and on psalteries, and on timbrels, and on cornets, and on cymbals.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And when they came to Nakhon’s <char style="add">[prepared]</char> threshing floor, ‘Uzah <char style="add">[strength]</char> put forth <char style="add">[his hand]</char> to the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and took hold of it; for the oxen shook <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the anger of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was kindled against ‘Uzah <char style="add">[strength]</char>; and God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> struck him there for <char style="add">[his]</char> error; and there he died by the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> was displeased, because the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had made a breach <char style="pn">(breaking forth; a break; opening, inlet)</char> upon ‘Uzah <char style="add">[strength]</char>: and he called the name of the place Peretz-’Uzah [breach <char style="pn">(breaking forth; a break; opening, inlet)</char> of strength] to this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> was afraid of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> that day, and said, How shall the ark of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> come to me?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />So David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> would not remove the ark of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> unto him into the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>: but David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> carried it aside into the house of ‘Oved-Edom <char style="add">[servant of Edom]</char> the Gitti <char style="add">[belonging to Gat (winepress)]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the ark of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> continued in the house of ‘Oved-Edom <char style="add">[servant of Edom]</char> the Gitti [belonging to Gat (winepress)] three months: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> ‘Oved-Edom <char style="add">[servant of Edom]</char>, and all his household.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And it was told king David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, saying, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> the house of ‘Oved-Edom <char style="add">[servant of Edom]</char>, and all that <char style="add">[pertains]</char> unto him, because of the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>. So David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> went and brought up the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> from the house of ‘Oved-Edom <char style="add">[servant of Edom]</char> into the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> with gladness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And it was <char style="add">[so]</char>, that when they that bore the ark of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had gone six paces, he sacrificed oxen and fatlings.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> danced before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> with all <char style="add">[his]</char> might; and David <char style="add">[beloved] [was]</char> girded with a linen ephod <char style="pn">(vest)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />So David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and all the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> brought up the ark of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> with shouting, and with the sound of the trumpet.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And as the ark of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came into the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, Mikhal <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> daughter looked through a window, and saw king David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> leaping and dancing before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; and she despised him in her heart.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And they brought in the ark of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and set it in his place, in the midst of the tabernacle that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> had pitched for it: and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> offered burnt offerings and peace offerings before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And as soon as David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> had made an end of offering burnt offerings and peace offerings, he Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> the people in the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And he dealt among all the people, <char style="add">[even]</char> among the whole multitude of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, as well to the women as men, to everyone a cake of bread, and a good piece <char style="add">[of flesh]</char>, and raisin cakes. So all the people departed everyone to his house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Then David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> returned to bless his household. And Mikhal <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> the daughter of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> came out to meet David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and said, How glorious was the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to day, who uncovered himself to day in the eyes of the handmaids of his servants, as one of the vain fellows shamelessly uncovers himself!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto Mikhal <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char>, <char style="add">[It was]</char> before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, which chose me before you<char style="ord">i</char> father, and before all his house, to appoint me ruler over the people of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: therefore will I play before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And I will yet be more vile than thus, and will be base in my own sight: and of the maidservants which you<char style="ord">i</char> have spoken of, of them shall I be had in honour.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Therefore Mikhal <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> the daughter of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> had no child unto the day of her death.</para>
  <chapter number="7" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass, when the king sat in his house, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had given him rest round about from all his enemies;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />That the king said unto Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char> the prophet, See now, I dwell in an house of cedar, but the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> dwells within curtains.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char> said to the king, Go, do all that <char style="add">[is]</char> in you<char style="ord">i</char> heart; for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And it came to pass that night, that the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Go and tell my servant David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, Shalt you<char style="ord">i</char> build me an house for me to dwell in?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Whereas I have not dwelt in <char style="add">[any]</char> house since the time that I brought up the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, even to this day, but have walked in a tent and in a tabernacle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />In all <char style="add">[the places]</char> wherein I have walked with all the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> spoke I a word with any of the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, whom I commanded to feed my people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, saying, Why build you<char style="ord">2f</char> not me an house of cedar?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Now therefore so shall you<char style="ord">i</char> say unto my servant David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, I took you<char style="ord">i</char> from the stable, from following the sheep, to be ruler over my people, over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And I was with you<char style="ord">i</char> to wherever you<char style="ord">i</char> went, and have cut off all your<char style="ord">i</char> enemies out of you<char style="ord">i</char> sight, and have made you<char style="ord">i</char> a great name, like unto the name of the great <char style="add">[men]</char> that <char style="add">[are]</char> in the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Moreover I will appoint a place for my people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and will plant them, that they may dwell in a place of their own, and move no more; neither shall the children of wickedness afflict them anymore, as formerly,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And as since the time that I commanded <char style="add">[to be]</char> over my people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and have caused you<char style="ord">i</char> to rest from all your<char style="ord">i</char> enemies. Also the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> tells you<char style="ord">i</char> that he will make you<char style="ord">i</char> an house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And when you<char style="ord">i</char> days be fulfilled, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall sleep with you<char style="ord">i</char> fathers, I will set up you<char style="ord">i</char> seed after you<char style="ord">i</char>, which shall proceed out of you<char style="ord">i</char> bowels <char style="pn">(inward parts; affections)</char>, and I will establish his kingdom.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />He shall build an house for my name, and I will establish the throne of his kingdom forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />I will be his father, and he shall be my son. If he commit iniquity, I will chasten him with the rod of men, and with the stripes of the children of men:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />But my mercy shall not depart away from him, as I took <char style="add">[it]</char> from Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, whom I put away before you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> house and you<char style="ord">i</char> kingdom shall be established forever before you<char style="ord">i</char>: your<char style="ord">i</char> throne shall be established forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />According to all these words, and according to all this vision, so did Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char> speak unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Then went king David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> in, and sat before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and he said, Who <char style="add">[am]</char> I, O Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>? and what <char style="add">[is]</char> my house, that you<char style="ord">i</char> have brought me up to this time?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And this was yet a small thing in you<char style="ord">i</char> sight, O Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; but you<char style="ord">i</char> have spoken also of your<char style="ord">i</char> servant’s house for a great while to come. And <char style="add">[is]</char> this the manner of man, O Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And what can David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> say more unto you<char style="ord">i</char>? for you<char style="ord">i</char>, Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, know your<char style="ord">i</char> servant.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />For your<char style="ord">i</char> word’s sake, and according to your<char style="ord">i</char> own heart, have you<char style="ord">i</char> done all these great things, to make your<char style="ord">i</char> servant know <char style="add">[them]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />For what reason you<char style="ord">i</char> are great, O Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>: for <char style="add">[there is]</char> none like you<char style="ord">i</char>, neither <char style="add">[is there any]</char> God-Elōhīm beside you<char style="ord">i</char>, according to all that we have heard with our ears.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And what one nation in the earth <char style="add">[is]</char> like your<char style="ord">i</char> people, <char style="add">[even]</char> like Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, whom God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> went to redeem for a people to himself, and to make him a name, and to do for you great things and terrible, for your<char style="ord">i</char> land, before your<char style="ord">i</char> people, which you<char style="ord">i</char> redeem to you<char style="ord">i</char> from Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, <char style="add">[from]</char> the nations and their gods?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />For you<char style="ord">i</char> have confirmed to yourself your<char style="ord">i</char> people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God] [to be]</char> a people unto you<char style="ord">i</char> forever: and you<char style="ord">i</char>, LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, are become their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And now, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, the word that you<char style="ord">i</char> have spoken concerning your<char style="ord">i</char> servant, and concerning his house, establish <char style="add">[it]</char> forever, and do as you<char style="ord">i</char> have said.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And let your<char style="ord">i</char> name be magnified forever, saying, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies] [is]</char> the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and let the house of your<char style="ord">i</char> servant David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> be established before you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />For you<char style="ord">i</char>, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, have revealed to your<char style="ord">i</char> servant, saying, I will build you<char style="ord">i</char> an house: therefore has your<char style="ord">i</char> servant found in his heart to pray this prayer unto you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And now, O Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> that God-Elōhīm and your<char style="ord">i</char> words be true, and you<char style="ord">i</char> have promised this goodness unto your<char style="ord">i</char> servant:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />Therefore now let it please you<char style="ord">i</char> to bless the house of your<char style="ord">i</char> servant, that it may continue forever before you<char style="ord">i</char>: for you<char style="ord">i</char>, O Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, have spoken <char style="add">[it]</char>: and with your<char style="ord">i</char> blessing let the house of your<char style="ord">i</char> servant be Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> forever.</para>
  <chapter number="8" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And after this it came to pass, that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> struck the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and subdued them: and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> took Meteg-Amah <char style="add">[mother city]</char> out of the hand of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he struck Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>, and measured them with a line, casting them down to the ground; even with two lines measured he to put to death, and with one full line to keep alive. And <char style="add">[so]</char> the Mo’avi <char style="add">[of his father]</char> became David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s servants, <char style="add">[and]</char> brought gifts.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> struck also Hadad’ezer <char style="add">[mighty’meaning disputed]</char>, the son of Rechov <char style="add">[Broad Place]</char>, king of Tzovah <char style="add">[station]</char>, as he went to recover his border at the river Euphrates <char style="pn">(to break forth, to gush)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> took from him a thousand <char style="add">[chariots]</char>, and seven hundred horsemen, and twenty thousand footmen: and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> hamstringed all the chariot <char style="add">[horses]</char>, but reserved of them <char style="add">[for]</char> an hundred chariots.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And when the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> of Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char> came to aid Hadad’ezer <char style="add">[mighty - meaning disputed]</char> king of Tzovah <char style="add">[station]</char>, David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> killed of the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> two and twenty thousand men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Then David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> put garrisons in Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> f Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char>: and the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> became servants to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> brought gifts. And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> preserved David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> to wherever he went.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> took the shields of gold that were on the servants of Hadad’ezer <char style="add">[mighty - meaning disputed]</char>, and brought them to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And from Betach <char style="add">[security]</char>, and from Berotai <char style="add">[cypress grove]</char>, cities of Hadad’ezer <char style="add">[mighty - meaning disputed]</char>, king David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> took exceeding much brass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />When To’i <char style="add">[wander]</char> king of Hamat <char style="add">[Fortress]</char> heard that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> had smitten all the host of Hadad’ezer <char style="add">[mighty - meaning disputed]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Then To’i <char style="add">[wander]</char> sent Yoram <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> his son unto king David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, to salute him, and to bless him, because he had fought against Hadad’ezer <char style="add">[mighty - meaning disputed]</char>, and smitten him: for Hadad’ezer <char style="add">[mighty - meaning disputed]</char> had wars with To’i <char style="add">[wander]</char>. And <char style="add">[Yoram [Yehovah is exalted]]</char> brought with him vessels of silver, and vessels of gold, and vessels of brass:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Which also king David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> did dedicate unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, with the silver and gold that he had dedicated of all nations which he subdued;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>, and of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>, and of the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, and of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and of ‘Amalek <char style="add">[Dweller in a Valley]</char>, and of the spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> of Hadad’ezer <char style="add">[mighty - meaning disputed]</char>, son of Rechov <char style="add">[Broad Place]</char>, king of Tzovah <char style="add">[station]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> got <char style="add">[him]</char> a name when he returned from attacking of the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> in the valley of salt, <char style="add">[being]</char> eighteen thousand <char style="add">[men]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And he put garrisons in Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>; throughout all Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char> put he garrisons, and all they of Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char> became David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s servants. And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> preserved David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> to wherever he went.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> reigned over all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> executed judgment and justice unto all his people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> the son of Tz’ruyah <char style="add">[balsam] [was]</char> over the host; and Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> the son of Achilud [child’s brother] <char style="add">[was]</char> recorder;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> the son of Achituv <char style="add">[my brother is good]</char>, and Achi-Melekh <char style="add">[my brother is king]</char> the son of Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great]</char>, <char style="add">[were]</char> the priests; and S’rayah <char style="add">[Yehovah is ruler] [was]</char> the scribe;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And B’nayahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has built]</char> the son of Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows] [was over]</char> both the K’reti <char style="add">[executioners]</char> and the P’leti <char style="add">[couriers]</char>; and David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s sons were chief rulers.</para>
  <chapter number="9" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said, Is there yet any that is left of the house of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, that I may show him kindness for Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>’s sake?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And <char style="add">[there was]</char> of the house of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> a servant whose name <char style="add">[was]</char> Tziva <char style="add">[statue]</char>. And when they had called him unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, the king said unto him, <char style="add">[Are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> Tziva <char style="add">[statue]</char>? And he said, Your<char style="ord">1s</char> servant <char style="add">[is he]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the king said, <char style="add">[Is]</char> there not yet any of the house of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, that I may show the kindness of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> unto him? And Tziva <char style="add">[statue]</char> said unto the king, Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> has yet a son, <char style="add">[which is]</char> lame on <char style="add">[his]</char> feet.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the king said unto him, Where <char style="add">[is]</char> he? And Tziva <char style="add">[statue]</char> said unto the king, Behold, he <char style="add">[is]</char> in the house of Makhir <char style="add">[Sold]</char>, the son of ‘Ammi’el <char style="add">[my kinsman is God] [My Kinsman is God]</char>, in Lo-D’var <char style="add">[not a pasture]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Then king David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> sent, and fetched him out of the house of Makhir <char style="add">[Sold]</char>, the son of ‘Ammi’el <char style="add">[my kinsman is God] [My Kinsman is God]</char>, from Lo-D’var <char style="add">[not a pasture]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Now when M’fivoshet <char style="add">[exterminating the idol]</char>, the son of Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>, the son of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, was come unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, he fell on his face, and did reverence. And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said, M’fivoshet <char style="add">[exterminating the idol]</char>. And he answered, Behold you<char style="ord">i</char> servant!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto him, Fear not: for I will surely show you<char style="ord">i</char> kindness for Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> father’s sake, and will restore you<char style="ord">i</char> all the land of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> father; and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall eat bread at my table continually.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And he bowed himself, and said, What <char style="add">[is]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> servant, that you<char style="ord">i</char> should look upon such a dead dog as I <char style="add">[am]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Then the king called to Tziva <char style="add">[statue]</char>, Sha’ul’s <char style="add">[desired]</char> servant, and said unto him, I have given unto your<char style="ord">i</char> master’s son all that pertained to Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and to all his house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> therefore, and your<char style="ord">i</char> sons, and your<char style="ord">i</char> servants, shall till the land for him, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall bring in <char style="add">[the fruits]</char>, that your<char style="ord">i</char> master’s son may have food to eat: but M’fivoshet <char style="add">[exterminating the idol]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> master’s son shall eat bread always at my table. Now Tziva <char style="add">[statue]</char> had fifteen sons and twenty servants.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Then said Tziva <char style="add">[statue]</char> unto the king, According to all that my lord the king has commanded his servant, so shall your<char style="ord">i</char> servant do. As for M’fivoshet <char style="add">[exterminating the idol]</char>, <char style="add">[said the king]</char>, he shall eat at my table, as one of the king’s sons.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And M’fivoshet <char style="add">[exterminating the idol]</char> had a young son, whose name <char style="add">[was]</char> Mikha <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char>. And all that dwelt in the house of Tziva <char style="add">[statue] [were]</char> servants unto M’fivoshet <char style="add">[exterminating the idol]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />So M’fivoshet <char style="add">[exterminating the idol]</char> dwelt in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: for he did eat continually at the king’s table; and was lame on both his feet.</para>
  <chapter number="10" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass after this, that the king of the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> died, and Hanun <char style="add">[gracious]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Then said David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, I will show kindness unto Hanun <char style="add">[gracious]</char> the son of Nachash <char style="add">[serpent]</char>, as his father showed kindness unto me. And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> sent to comfort him by the hand of his servants for his father. And David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s servants came into the land of the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the princes of the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> said unto Hanun <char style="add">[gracious]</char> their lord, Think you<char style="ord">i</char> that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> does honour your<char style="ord">i</char> father, that he has sent comforters unto you<char style="ord">i</char>? has not David <char style="add">[beloved] [rather]</char> sent his servants unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, to search the city, and to spy it out, and to overthrow it?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />For what reason Hanun <char style="add">[gracious]</char> took David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s servants, and shaved off the one half of their beards, and cut off their garments in the middle, <char style="add">[even]</char> to their buttocks, and sent them away.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />When they told <char style="add">[it]</char> unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, he sent to meet them, because the men were greatly ashamed: and the king said, Tarry at Yericho <char style="add">[Its Moon]</char> until your beards be grown, and <char style="add">[then]</char> return.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And when the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> saw that they stank before David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> sent and hired the children of Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> of Beit-Rechov <char style="add">[House of the Street]</char>, and the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> of Tzovah <char style="add">[station]</char>, twenty thousand footmen, and of king Ma’akhah <char style="add">[oppression] [oppression]</char> a thousand men, and of Ish-Tov <char style="add">[man of goodness]</char> twelve thousand men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And when David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> heard of <char style="add">[it]</char>, he sent Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, and all the host of the mighty men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> came out, and put the battle in array <char style="pn">(to put on; to clothe)</char> at the entering in of the gate: and the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> of Tzovah <char style="add">[station]</char>, and of Rechov <char style="add">[Broad Place]</char>, and Ish-Tov <char style="add">[man of goodness]</char>, and Ma’akhah <char style="add">[oppression] [oppression]</char>, <char style="add">[were]</char> by themselves in the field.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />When Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> saw that the front of the battle was against him before and behind, he chose of all the choice <char style="add">[men]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and put <char style="add">[them]</char> in array <char style="pn">(to put on; to clothe)</char> against the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the rest of the people he delivered into the hand of Avishai <char style="add">[my father is a gift]</char> his brother, that he might put <char style="add">[them]</char> in array <char style="pn">(to put on; to clothe)</char> against the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And he said, If the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> be too strong for me, then you<char style="ord">i</char> shall help me: but if the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> be too strong for you<char style="ord">i</char>, then I will come and help you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Be of good courage, and let us play the men for our people, and for the cities of our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> do that which seems him good.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> drew near, and the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him, unto the battle against the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char>: and they fled before him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And when the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> saw that the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> were fled, then fled they also before Avishai <char style="add">[my father is a gift]</char>, and entered into the city. So Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> returned from the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, and came to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And when the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> saw that they were smitten before Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, they gathered themselves together.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And Hadad’ezer <char style="add">[mighty - meaning disputed]</char> is help sent, and brought out the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> that <char style="add">[were]</char> beyond the river: and they came to Heilam <char style="add">[stronghold]</char>; and Shovakh <char style="add">[expansion]</char> the captain of the host of Hadad’ezer <char style="add">[mighty - meaning disputed]</char> is help <char style="add">[went]</char> before them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And when it was told David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, he gathered all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> together, and passed over Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>, and came to Heilam <char style="add">[stronghold]</char>. And the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> set themselves in array <char style="pn">(to put on; to clothe)</char> against David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and fought with him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> fled before Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> killed <char style="add">[the men of]</char> seven hundred chariots of the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char>, and forty thousand horsemen, and struck Shovakh <char style="add">[expansion]</char> the captain of their host, who died there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And when all the kings <char style="add">[that were]</char> servants to Hadad’ezer <char style="add">[mighty - meaning disputed]</char> is help saw that they were smitten before Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, they made peace with Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and served them. So the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> feared to help the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> any more.</para>
  <chapter number="11" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass, after the year was expired, at the time when kings go forth <char style="add">[to battle]</char>, that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> sent Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, and his servants with him, and all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and they destroyed the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, and besieged Rabbah <char style="add">[Great]</char>. But David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> tarried still at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And it came to pass in an evening, that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> arose from off his bed, and walked upon the roof of the king’s house: and from the roof he saw a woman washing herself; and the woman <char style="add">[was]</char> very beautiful to look upon.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> sent and enquired after the woman. And <char style="add">[one]</char> said, <char style="add">[Is]</char> not this Bat-Sheva <char style="add">[daughter of an oath]</char>, the daughter of Eli’am <char style="add">[God of the people, or God is kinsman]</char>, the wife of Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my light (flame)]</char> the Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> sent messengers, and took her; and she came in unto him, and he lay with her; for she was purified from her uncleanness: and she returned unto her house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the woman conceived, and sent and told David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and said, I <char style="add">[am]</char> with child.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> sent to Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, <char style="add">[saying]</char>, Send me Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my light (flame)]</char> the Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char>. And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> sent Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my light (flame)]</char> to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And when Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my light (flame)]</char> was come unto him, David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> demanded <char style="add">[of him]</char> how Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> did, and how the people did, and how the war prospered.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said to Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my light (flame)]</char>, Go down to you<char style="ord">i</char> house, and wash you<char style="ord">i</char> feet. And Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my light (flame)]</char> departed out of the king’s house, and there followed him a mess <char style="add">[of meat]</char> from the king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />But Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my light (flame)]</char> slept at the door of the king’s house with all the servants of his lord, and went not down to his house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And when they had told David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, saying, Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my light (flame)]</char> went not down unto his house, David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my light (flame)]</char>, came you<char style="ord">i</char> not from <char style="add">[your<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> journey? why <char style="add">[then]</char> did you<char style="ord">i</char> not go down unto your<char style="ord">i</char> house?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my light (flame)]</char> said unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, The ark, and Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, abide in tents; and my lord Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, and the servants of my lord, are encamped in the open fields; shall I then go into my house, to eat and to drink, and to lie with my wife? <char style="add">[as]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> live, and <char style="add">[as]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> soul lives, I will not do this thing.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said to Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my light (flame)]</char>, Tarry here today also, and tomorrow I will let you<char style="ord">i</char> depart. So Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my light (flame)]</char> abode in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> that day, and the morrow.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And when David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> had called him, he did eat and drink before him; and he made him drunk: and at even he went out to lie on his bed with the servants of his lord, but went not down to his house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And it came to pass in the morning, that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> wrote a letter to Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, and sent <char style="add">[it]</char> by the hand of Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my light (flame)]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And he wrote in the letter, saying, Set you<char style="ord">2f</char> Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my light (flame)]</char> in the forefront of the hottest battle, and retire you<char style="ord">2f</char> from him, that he may be smitten, and die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And it came to pass, when Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> observed the city, that he assigned Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my light (flame)]</char> unto a place where he knew that valiant men <char style="add">[were]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the men of the city went out, and fought with Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>: and there fell <char style="add">[some]</char> of the people of the servants of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>; and Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my light (flame)]</char> the Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char> died also.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Then Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> sent and told David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> all the things concerning the war;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And charged the messenger, saying, When you<char style="ord">i</char> have made an end of telling the matters of the war unto the king,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And if so be that the king’s wrath arise, and he say unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, For what reason approached you<char style="ord">2f</char> so near unto the city when you<char style="ord">2f</char> did fight? knew you<char style="ord">2f</char> not that they would shoot from the wall?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Who struck Avi-Melekh <char style="add">[My Father is King]</char> the son of Yerubeshet <char style="add">[shame will contend]</char>? did not a woman cast a piece of a millstone upon him from the wall, that he died in Tevetz <char style="add">[Conspicuous]</char>? why went you<char style="ord">2f</char> near the wall? then say you<char style="ord">i</char>, Your<char style="ord">1s</char> servant Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my light (flame)]</char> the Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char> is dead also.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />So the messenger went, and came and showed David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> all that Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> had sent him for.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And the messenger said unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, Surely the men prevailed against us, and came out unto us into the field, and we were upon them even unto the entering of the gate.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And the shooters shot from off the wall upon your<char style="ord">i</char> servants; and <char style="add">[some]</char> of the king’s servants be dead, and your<char style="ord">i</char> servant Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my light (flame)]</char> the Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char> is dead also.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Then David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto the messenger, Thus shall you<char style="ord">i</char> say unto Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, Let not this thing displease you<char style="ord">i</char>, for the sword devours one as well as another: make your<char style="ord">i</char> battle more strong against the city, and overthrow it: and encourage you<char style="ord">i</char> him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And when the wife of Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my light (flame)]</char> heard that Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my light (flame)]</char> her husband was dead, she mourned for her husband.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And when the mourning was past, David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> sent and fetched her to his house, and she became his wife, and bore him a son. But the thing that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> had done displeased the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="12" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> sent Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char> unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>. And he came unto him, and said unto him, There were two men in one city; the one rich, and the other poor.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />The rich <char style="add">[man]</char> had exceeding many flocks and herds:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />But the poor <char style="add">[man]</char> had nothing, save one little ewe lamb, which he had bought and nourished up: and it grew up together with him, and with his children; it did eat of his own meat, and drank of his own cup, and lay in his bosom, and was unto him as a daughter.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And there came a traveller unto the rich man, and he spared to take of his own flock and of his own herd, to dress for the wayfaring man that was come unto him; but took the poor man’s lamb, and dressed it for the man that was come to him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s anger was greatly kindled against the man; and he said to Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char>, <char style="add">[As]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives, the man that has done this <char style="add">[thing]</char> shall surely die:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he shall restore the lamb fourfold, because he did this thing, and because he had no pity.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char> said to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> the man. Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, I anointed you<char style="ord">i</char> king over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and I delivered you<char style="ord">i</char> out of the hand of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And I gave you<char style="ord">i</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> master’s house, and your<char style="ord">i</char> master’s wives into your<char style="ord">i</char> bosom, and gave you<char style="ord">i</char> the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>; and if <char style="add">[that had been]</char> too little, I would moreover have given unto you<char style="ord">i</char> such and such things.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />For what reason have you<char style="ord">i</char> despised the commandment of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, to do evil in his sight? you<char style="ord">i</char> have killed Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my light (flame)]</char> the Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char> with the sword, and have taken his wife <char style="add">[to be]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> wife, and have slain him with the sword of the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Now therefore the sword shall never depart from your<char style="ord">i</char> house; because you<char style="ord">i</char> have despised me, and have taken the wife of Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my light (flame)]</char> the Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char> to be your<char style="ord">i</char> wife.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, Behold, I will raise up evil against you<char style="ord">i</char> out of your<char style="ord">i</char> own house, and I will take your<char style="ord">i</char> wives before you<char style="ord">i</char> eyes, and give <char style="add">[them]</char> unto your<char style="ord">i</char> neighbour, and he shall lie with your<char style="ord">i</char> wives in the sight of this sun.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />For you<char style="ord">i</char> did <char style="add">[it]</char> secretly: but I will do this thing before all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and before the sun.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char>, I have sinned against the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. And Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char> said unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> also has put away your<char style="ord">i</char> sin; you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />However, because by this deed you<char style="ord">i</char> have given great occasion to the enemies of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> to blaspheme, the child also <char style="add">[that is]</char> born unto you<char style="ord">i</char> shall surely die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char> departed unto his house. And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> struck the child that Uriyah’s [Yehovah is my light (flame)]’s wife bore unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and it was very sick.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> therefore besought God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> for the child; and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> fasted, and went in, and lay all night upon the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the elders of his house arose, <char style="add">[and went]</char> to him, to raise him up from the earth: but he would not, neither did he eat bread with them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And it came to pass on the seventh day, that the child died. And the servants of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> feared to tell him that the child was dead: for they said, Behold, while the child was yet alive, we spoke unto him, and he would not hearken unto our voice: how will he then vex himself, if we tell him that the child is dead?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />But when David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> saw that his servants whispered, David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> perceived that the child was dead: therefore David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto his servants, Is the child dead? And they said, He is dead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Then David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> arose from the earth, and washed, and anointed <char style="add">[himself]</char>, and changed his apparel, and came into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and worshipped: then he came to his own house; and when he required, they set bread before him, and he did eat.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Then said his servants unto him, What thing <char style="add">[is]</char> this that you<char style="ord">i</char> have done? you<char style="ord">i</char> did fast and weep for the child, <char style="add">[while it was]</char> alive; but when the child was dead, you<char style="ord">i</char> did rise and eat bread.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And he said, While the child was yet alive, I fasted and wept: for I said, Who can tell <char style="add">[whether]</char> GOD will be gracious to me, that the child may live?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />But now he is dead, wherefore should I fast? can I bring him back again? I shall go to him, but he shall not return to me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> comforted Bat-Sheva <char style="add">[daughter of an oath]</char> his wife, and went in unto her, and lay with her: and she bore a son, and he called his name Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> loved him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And he sent by the hand of Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char> the prophet; and he called his name Y’didyah <char style="add">[beloved of Yehovah]</char>, because of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> fought against Rabbah <char style="add">[Great]</char> of the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, and took the royal city.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> sent messengers to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and said, I have fought against Rabbah <char style="add">[Great]</char>, and have taken the city of waters.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Now therefore gather the rest of the people together, and encamp against the city, and take it: lest I take the city, and it be called after my name.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> gathered all the people together, and went to Rabbah <char style="add">[Great]</char>, and fought against it, and took it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And he took their king’s crown from off his head, the weight whereof <char style="add">[was]</char> a talent <char style="pn">(weight of money; weight; gift)</char> of gold with the precious stones: and it was <char style="add">[set]</char> on David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s head. And he brought forth the spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> of the city in great abundance.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And he brought forth the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> in it, and put <char style="add">[them]</char> under saws, and under harrows of iron, and under axes of iron, and made them pass through the brick factory: and thus did he unto all the cities of the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>. So David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and all the people returned unto Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="13" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass after this, that Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> the son of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> had a fair sister, whose name <char style="add">[was]</char> Tamar <char style="add">[palm-tree]</char>; and Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char> the son of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> loved her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char> was so vexed, that he fell sick for his sister Tamar <char style="add">[palm-tree]</char>; for she <char style="add">[was]</char> a virgin; and Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char> thought it hard for him to do anything to her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />But Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char> had a friend, whose name <char style="add">[was]</char> Yonadav <char style="add">[Yehovah is willing] [Generous]</char>, the son of Shim’ah <char style="add">[report]</char> David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s brother: and Yonadav <char style="add">[Yehovah is willing] [Generous] [was]</char> a very subtle man.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And he said unto him, Why <char style="add">[are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="add">[being]</char> the king’s son, lean from day to day? will you<char style="ord">i</char> not tell me? And Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char> said unto him, I love Tamar <char style="add">[palm-tree]</char>, my brother Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>’s sister.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And Yonadav <char style="add">[Yehovah is willing] [Generous]</char> said unto him, Lay you<char style="ord">i</char> down on your<char style="ord">i</char> bed, and make yourself sick: and when your<char style="ord">i</char> father comes to see you<char style="ord">i</char>, say unto him, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, let my sister Tamar <char style="add">[palm-tree]</char> come, and give me meat, and dress the meat in my sight, that I may see <char style="add">[it]</char>, and eat <char style="add">[it]</char> at her hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />So Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char> lay down, and made himself sick: and when the king was come to see him, Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char> said unto the king, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, let Tamar <char style="add">[palm-tree]</char> my sister come, and make me a couple of cakes in my sight, that I may eat at her hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Then David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> sent home to Tamar <char style="add">[palm-tree]</char>, saying, Go now to your<char style="ord">i</char> brother Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char>’s house, and dress him meat.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />So Tamar <char style="add">[palm-tree]</char> went to her brother Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char>’s house; and he was laid down. And she took flour, and kneaded <char style="add">[it]</char>, and made cakes in his sight, and did bake the cakes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And she took a pan, and poured <char style="add">[them]</char> out before him; but he refused to eat. And Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char> said, Have out all men from me. And they went out every man from him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char> said unto Tamar <char style="add">[palm-tree]</char>, Bring the meat into the chamber, that I may eat of you<char style="ord">i</char> hand. And Tamar <char style="add">[palm-tree]</char> took the cakes which she had made, and brought <char style="add">[them]</char> into the chamber to Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char> her brother.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And when she had brought <char style="add">[them]</char> unto him to eat, he took hold of her, and said unto her, Come lie with me, my sister.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And she answered him, No, my brother, do not force me; for no such thing ought to be done in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: do not you<char style="ord">i</char> this folly.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And I, to which shall I cause my shame to go? and as for you<char style="ord">i</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be as one of the fools in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>. Now therefore, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, speak unto the king; for he will not withhold me from you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />However he would not hearken unto her voice: but, being stronger than she, forced her, and lay with her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Then Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char> hated her exceedingly; so that the hatred which he hated her <char style="add">[was]</char> greater than the love which he had loved her. And Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char> said unto her, Arise, be gone.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And she said unto him, <char style="add">[There is]</char> no cause: this evil in sending me away <char style="add">[is]</char> greater than the other that you<char style="ord">i</char> did unto me. But he would not hearken unto her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Then he called his servant that ministered unto him, and said, Put now this <char style="add">[woman]</char> out from me, and bolt the door after her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And <char style="add">[she had]</char> a garment of diverse colours upon her: for with such robes were the king’s daughters <char style="add">[that were]</char> virgins appareled. Then his servant brought her out, and bolted the door after her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And Tamar <char style="add">[palm-tree]</char> put ashes on her head, and rent her garment of diverse colours that <char style="add">[was]</char> on her, and laid her hand on her head, and went on crying.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> her brother said unto her, Has Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> brother been with you<char style="ord">i</char>? but hold now you<char style="ord">i</char> peace, my sister: he <char style="add">[is]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> brother; regard not this thing. So Tamar <char style="add">[palm-tree]</char> remained desolate in her brother Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>’s house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />But when king David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> heard of all these things, he was very exceedingly angry.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> spoke unto his brother Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char> neither good nor bad: for Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> hated Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char>, because he had forced his sister Tamar <char style="add">[palm-tree]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And it came to pass after two full years, that Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> had sheepshearers in Ba’al-Hatzor <char style="add">[lord of the village]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> beside Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>: and Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> invited all the king’s sons.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> came to the king, and said, Behold now, your<char style="ord">i</char> servant has sheepshearers; let the king, I beseech <char style="pn">(to call upon; appeal; beg)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>, and his servants go with you<char style="ord">i</char> servant.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And the king said to Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>, No, my son, let us not all now go, lest we be chargeable unto you<char style="ord">i</char>. And he pressed him: howbeit he would not go, but Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Then said Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>, If not, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, let my brother Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char> go with us. And the king said unto him, Why should he go with you<char style="ord">i</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />But Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> pressed him, that he let Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char> and all the king’s sons go with him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Now Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> had commanded his servants, saying, Mark you<char style="ord">2f</char> now when Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char>’s heart is merry with wine, and when I say unto you, Strike Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char>; then kill him, fear not: have not I commanded you? be courageous, and be valiant.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And the servants of Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> did unto Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char> as Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> had commanded. Then all the king’s sons arose, and every man got him up upon his mule, and fled.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And it came to pass, while they were in the way, that tidings came to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, saying, Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> has slain all the king’s sons, and there is not one of them left.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />Then the king arose, and tare his garments, and lay on the earth; and all his servants stood by with their clothes rent.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And Yonadav <char style="add">[Yehovah is willing] [Generous]</char>, the son of Shim’ah <char style="add">[report]</char> David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s brother, answered and said, Let not my lord suppose <char style="add">[that]</char> they have slain all the young men the king’s sons; for Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char> only is dead: for by the appointment of Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> this has been determined from the day that he forced his sister Tamar <char style="add">[palm-tree]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />Now therefore let not my lord the king take the thing to his heart, to think that all the king’s sons are dead: for Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char> only is dead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />But Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> fled. And the young man that kept the watch lifted up his eyes, and looked, and, behold, there came much people by the way of the hill side behind him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And Yonadav <char style="add">[Yehovah is willing] [Generous]</char> said unto the king, Behold, the king’s sons come: as your<char style="ord">i</char> servant said, so it is.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And it came to pass, as soon as he had made an end of speaking, that, behold, the king’s sons came, and lifted up their voice and wept: and the king also and all his servants wept very sore.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />But Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> fled, and went to Talmai <char style="add">[Plowman]</char>, the son of Ammihud <char style="add">[People of Majesty]</char>, king of G’shur <char style="add">[proud beholder]</char>. And [David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>] mourned for his son every day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />So Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> fled, and went to G’shur <char style="add">[proud beholder]</char>, and was there three years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />And <char style="add">[the soul of]</char> king David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> longed to go forth unto Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>: for he was comforted concerning Amnon <char style="add">[faithful]</char>, seeing he was dead.</para>
  <chapter number="14" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> the son of Tz’ruyah <char style="add">[balsam]</char> perceived that the king’s heart <char style="add">[was]</char> toward Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> sent to T’koa <char style="add">[trumpet blast]</char>, and fetched there a wise woman, and said unto her, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, feign <char style="pn">(to pretend to be; to disguise)</char> yourself to be a mourner, and put on now mourning apparel, and anoint not yourself with oil, but be as a woman that had a long time mourned for the dead:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And come to the king, and speak on this manner unto him. So Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> put the words in her mouth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And when the woman of T’koa <char style="add">[trumpet blast]</char> spoke to the king, she fell on her face to the ground, and did obesiance <char style="pn">(bowing or kneeling in respect)</char>, and said, Help, O king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the king said unto her, What ails you<char style="ord">i</char>? And she answered, I <char style="add">[am]</char> indeed a widow woman, and my husband is dead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And your<char style="ord">i</char> female servant had two sons, and they two strove together in the field, and <char style="add">[there was]</char> none to part them, but the one struck the other, and killed him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And, behold, the whole family is risen against your<char style="ord">i</char> female servant, and they said, Deliver him that struck his brother, that we may kill him, for the life of his brother whom he killed; and we will destroy the heir also: and so they shall quench my coal which is left, and shall not leave to my husband <char style="add">[neither]</char> name nor remainder upon the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And the king said unto the woman, Go to your<char style="ord">i</char> house, and I will give charge concerning you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And the woman of T’koa <char style="add">[trumpet blast]</char> said unto the king, My lord, O king, the iniquity <char style="add">[be]</char> on me, and on my father’s house: and the king and his throne <char style="add">[be]</char> guiltless.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the king said, Whosoever says <char style="add">[ought]</char> unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, bring him to me, and he shall not touch you<char style="ord">i</char> anymore.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Then said she, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, let the king remember the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, that you<char style="ord">i</char> would not suffer the revengers of blood to destroy any more, lest they destroy my son. And he said, <char style="add">[As]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives, there shall not one hair of your<char style="ord">i</char> son fall to <char style="pn">(to do entirely, do wholly)</char> the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Then the woman said, Let your<char style="ord">i</char> female servant, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, speak <char style="add">[one]</char> word unto my lord the king. And he said, Say on.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the woman said, For what reason then have you<char style="ord">i</char> thought such a thing against the people of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>? for the king does speak this thing as one which is faulty, in that the king does not fetch home again his banished.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />For we must needs die, and <char style="add">[are]</char> as water spilt on the ground, which cannot be gathered up again; neither does God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> respect <char style="add">[any]</char> person: yet does he devise means, that his banished be not expelled from him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Now therefore that I am come to speak of this thing unto my lord the king, <char style="add">[it is]</char> because the people have made me afraid: and you<char style="ord">i</char> female servant said, I will now speak unto the king; it may be that the king will perform the request of his female servant.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />For the king will hear, to deliver his female servant out of the hand of the man <char style="add">[that would]</char> destroy me and my son together out of the inheritance of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Then your<char style="ord">i</char> female servant said, The word of my lord the king shall now be comfortable: for as an angel of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, so <char style="add">[is]</char> my lord the king to discern good and bad: therefore the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> will be with you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Then the king answered and said unto the woman, Hide not from me, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, the thing that I shall ask you<char style="ord">i</char>. And the woman said, Let my lord the king now speak.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the king said, <char style="add">[Is not]</char> the hand of Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char> in all this? And the woman answered and said, <char style="add">[As]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> soul lives, my lord the king, none can turn to the right hand or to the left from ought that my lord the king has spoken: for your<char style="ord">i</char> servant Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, he bade me, and he put all these words in the mouth of your<char style="ord">i</char> female servant:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />To fetch about this form of speech has your<char style="ord">i</char> servant Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> done this thing: and my lord <char style="add">[is]</char> wise, according to the wisdom of an angel of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, to know all <char style="add">[things]</char> that <char style="add">[are]</char> in the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the king said unto Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, Behold now, I have done this thing: go therefore, bring the young man Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> again.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> fell to the ground on his face, and bowed himself, and thanked the king: and Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> said, To day your<char style="ord">i</char> servant knows that I have found grace in your<char style="ord">i</char> sight, my lord, O king, in that the king has fulfilled the request of his servant.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />So Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> arose and went to G’shur <char style="add">[proud beholder]</char>, and brought Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And the king said, Let him turn to his own house, and let him not see my face. So Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> returned to his own house, and saw not the king’s face.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />But in all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> there was none to be so much praised as Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> for his beauty: from the sole of his foot even to the crown of his head there was no blemish in him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And when he cut hair from his head, (for it was at every year’s end that he polled <char style="add">[it]</char>: because <char style="add">[the hair]</char> was heavy on him, therefore he polled it) he weighed the hair of his head at two hundred shekels after the king’s weight.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And unto Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> there were born three sons, and one daughter, whose name <char style="add">[was]</char> Tamar <char style="add">[palm-tree]</char>: she was a woman of a fair Countenance <char style="pn">(Face, appearance; show favor)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />So Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> dwelt two full years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and saw not the king’s face.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />Therefore Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> sent for Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, to have sent him to the king; but he would not come to him: and when he sent again the second time, he would not come.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />Therefore he said unto his servants, See, Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>’s field is near my, and he has barley there; go and set it on fire. And Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>’s servants set the field on fire.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />Then Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> arose, and came to Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> unto <char style="add">[his]</char> house, and said unto him, For what reason have you<char style="ord">i</char> servants set my field on fire?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> answered Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, Behold, I sent unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, saying, Come here, that I may send you<char style="ord">i</char> to the king, to say, For what reason am I come from G’shur <char style="add">[proud beholder]</char>? <char style="add">[it had been]</char> good for me <char style="add">[to have been]</char> there still: now therefore let me see the king’s face; and if there be <char style="add">[any]</char> iniquity in me, let him kill me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />So Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> came to the king, and told him: and when he had called for Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>, he came to the king, and bowed himself on his face to the ground before the king: and the king kissed Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="15" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass after this, that Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> prepared him chariots and horses, and fifty men to run before him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> rose up early, and stood beside the way of the gate: and it was <char style="add">[so]</char>, that when any man that had a controversy came to the king for judgment, then Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> called unto him, and said, Of what city <char style="add">[are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>? And he said, You<char style="ord">1s</char> servant <char style="add">[is]</char> of one of the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> said unto him, See, you<char style="ord">i</char> matters <char style="add">[are]</char> good and right; but <char style="add">[there is]</char> no man <char style="add">[deputed]</char> of the king to hear you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> said moreover, Oh that I were made judge in the land, that every man which has any suit or cause might come unto me, and I would do him justice!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And it was <char style="add">[so]</char>, that when any man came near <char style="add">[to him]</char> to do him obesiance <char style="pn">(bowing or kneeling in respect)</char>, he put forth his hand, and took him, and kissed him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And on this manner did Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> to all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> that came to the king for judgment: so Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> stole the hearts of the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And it came to pass after forty years, that Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> said unto the king, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, let me go and pay my vow, which I have vowed unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, in Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />For you<char style="ord">i</char> servant vowed a vow while I abode at G’shur <char style="add">[proud beholder]</char> in Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>, saying, If the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall bring me again indeed to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, then I will serve the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And the king said unto him, Go in peace. So he arose, and went to Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />But Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> sent spies throughout all the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, saying, As soon as you<char style="ord">2f</char> hear the sound of the trumpet, then you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall say, Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> reigns in Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And with Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> went two hundred men out of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, <char style="add">[that were]</char> called; and they went in their simplicity, and they knew not anything.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> sent for Achitofel <char style="add">[my brother i foolish]</char> the Giloni <char style="add">[gentilic of preceding]</char>, David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s counselor, from his city, <char style="add">[even]</char> from Giloh <char style="add">[Exile]</char>, while he offered sacrifices. And the conspiracy was strong; for the people increased continually with Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And there came a messenger to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, saying, The hearts of the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> are after Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto all his servants that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, Arise, and let us flee; for we shall not <char style="add">[else]</char> escape from Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>: make speed to depart, lest he overtake us suddenly, and bring evil upon us, and strike the city with the edge of the sword.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the king’s servants said unto the king, Behold, your<char style="ord">i</char> servants <char style="add">[are ready to do]</char> whatsoever my lord the king shall appoint.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And the king went forth, and all his household after him. And the king left ten women, <char style="add">[which were]</char> concubines, to keep the house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the king went forth, and all the people after him, and tarried in a place that was far off.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And all his servants passed on beside him; and all the K’reti <char style="add">[executioners]</char>, and all the P’leti <char style="add">[couriers]</char>, and all the Gittim <char style="add">[belonging to the winepress]</char>, six hundred men which came after him from Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char>, passed on before the king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Then said the king to Ittai <char style="add">[with me]</char> the Gitti <char style="add">[belonging to Gat (winepress)]</char>, For what reason go you<char style="ord">i</char> also with us? return to your<char style="ord">i</char> place, and abide with the king: for you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> a stranger, and also an exile.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Whereas you<char style="ord">i</char> came <char style="add">[but]</char> yesterday, should I this day make you<char style="ord">i</char> go up and down with us? seeing I go to which I may, return you<char style="ord">i</char>, and take back your<char style="ord">i</char> brethren: mercy and truth <char style="add">[be]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Ittai <char style="add">[with me]</char> answered the king, and said, <char style="add">[As]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives, and <char style="add">[as]</char> my lord the king lives, surely in what place my lord the king shall be, whether in death or life, even there also will your<char style="ord">i</char> servant be.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said to Ittai <char style="add">[with me]</char>, Go and pass over. And Ittai <char style="add">[with me]</char> the Gitti <char style="add">[belonging to Gat (winepress)]</char> passed over, and all his men, and all the little ones that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And all the country wept with a loud voice, and all the people passed over: the king also himself passed over the brook Kidron <char style="add">[dark]</char>, and all the people passed over, toward the way of the wilderness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And lo Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> also, and all the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to] [were]</char> with him, bearing the ark of the covenant of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>: and they set down the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>; and Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great]</char> went up, until all the people had done passing out of the city.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And the king said unto Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char>, Carry back the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> into the city: if I shall find favour in the eyes of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, he will bring me again, and show me <char style="add">[both]</char> it, and his habitation:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />But if he thus say, I have no delight in you<char style="ord">i</char>; behold, <char style="add">[here am]</char> I, let him do to me as seems good unto him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />The king said also unto Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> the priest, <char style="add">[Are not]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> a seer? return into the city in peace, and your two sons with you, Achima’atz <char style="add">[my brother is anger (wrath)]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> son, and Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> the son of Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />See, I will wait in the plain of the wilderness, until there come word from you to certify me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> therefore and Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great]</char> carried the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> again to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: and they tarried there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> went up by the ascent of <char style="add">[mount of]</char> Olives, and wept as he went up, and had his head covered, and he went barefoot: and all the people that <char style="add">[was]</char> with him covered every man his head, and they went up, weeping as they went up.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And <char style="add">[one]</char> told David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, saying, Achitofel <char style="add">[my brother i foolish] [is]</char> among the conspirators with Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>. And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, turn the counsel of Achitofel <char style="add">[my brother i foolish]</char> into foolishness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And it came to pass, that <char style="add">[when]</char> David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> was come to the top <char style="add">[of the mount]</char>, where he worshipped God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, behold, Hushai <char style="add">[hasting]</char> the Arki <char style="add">[lengthy]</char> came to meet him with his coat rent, and earth upon his head:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />Unto whom David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said, If you<char style="ord">i</char> pass on with me, then you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be a burden unto me:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />But if you<char style="ord">i</char> return to the city, and say unto Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>, I will be your<char style="ord">i</char> servant, O king; <char style="add">[as]</char> I <char style="add">[have been]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> father’s servant up to this time, so <char style="add">[will]</char> I now also <char style="add">[be]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> servant: then may you<char style="ord">i</char> for me defeat the counsel of Achitofel <char style="add">[my brother i foolish]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And <char style="add">[have you<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> not there with you<char style="ord">i</char> Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> and Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great]</char> the priests? therefore it shall be, <char style="add">[that]</char> what thing soever you<char style="ord">i</char> shall hear out of the king’s house, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall tell <char style="add">[it]</char> to Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> and Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great]</char> the priests.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />Behold, <char style="add">[they have]</char> there with them their two sons, Achima’atz [my brother is anger (wrath)] Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char>’s <char style="add">[son]</char>, and Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great]</char>’s <char style="add">[son]</char>; and by them you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall send unto me every thing that you<char style="ord">2f</char> can hear.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />So Hushai <char style="add">[hasting]</char> David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s friend came into the city, and Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> came into Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="16" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And when David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> was a little past the top <char style="add">[of the hill]</char>, behold, Tziva <char style="add">[statue]</char> the servant of M’fivoshet <char style="add">[exterminating the idol]</char> met him, with a couple of asses saddled, and upon them two hundred <char style="add">[loaves]</char> of bread, and an hundred bunches of raisins, and an hundred of summer fruits, and a bottle of wine.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the king said unto Tziva <char style="add">[statue]</char>, What mean you<char style="ord">i</char> by these? And Tziva <char style="add">[statue]</char> said, The asses <char style="add">[be]</char> for the king’s household to ride on; and the bread and summer fruit for the young men to eat; and the wine, that such as be faint in the wilderness may drink.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the king said, And where <char style="add">[is]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> master’s son? And Tziva <char style="add">[statue]</char> said unto the king, Behold, he abides at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: for he said, To day shall the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> restore me the kingdom of my father.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Then said the king to Tziva <char style="add">[statue]</char>, Behold, you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> all that <char style="add">[pertained]</char> unto M’fivoshet <char style="add">[exterminating the idol]</char>. And Tziva <char style="add">[statue]</char> said, I humbly beseech <char style="pn">(to call upon; appeal; beg)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[that]</char> I may find grace in you<char style="ord">i</char> sight, my lord, O king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And when king David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> came to Bachurim <char style="add">[young men’s village]</char>, behold, there came out a man of the family of the house of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, whose name <char style="add">[was]</char> Shime’i <char style="add">[Fame]</char>, the son of Gera <char style="add">[A Grain]</char>: he came forth, and cursed still as he came.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he cast stones at David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and at all the servants of king David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>: and all the people and all the mighty men <char style="add">[were]</char> on his right hand and on his left.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And thus said Shime’i <char style="add">[Fame]</char> when he cursed, Come out, come out, you<char style="ord">i</char> bloody man, and you<char style="ord">i</char> man of Belial <char style="add">[Worthless, Good for Nothing]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has returned upon you<char style="ord">i</char> all the blood of the house of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, in whose stead you<char style="ord">i</char> have reigned; and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has delivered the kingdom into the hand of Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> son: and, behold, you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are taken]</char> in you<char style="ord">i</char> mischief, because you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> a bloody man.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Then said Avishai <char style="add">[my father is a gift]</char> the son of Tz’ruyah <char style="add">[balsam]</char> unto the king, Why should this dead dog curse my lord the king? let me go over, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, and take off his head.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the king said, What have I to do with you, you<char style="ord">2f</char> sons of Tz’ruyah <char style="add">[balsam]</char>? so let him curse, because the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has said unto him, Curse David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>. Who shall then say, For what reason have you<char style="ord">i</char> done so?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said to Avishai <char style="add">[my father is a gift]</char>, and to all his servants, Behold, my son, which came forth of my bowels <char style="pn">(inward parts; affections)</char>, seeks my life: how much more now <char style="add">[may this]</char> Benyamini <char style="add">[son of the right hand] [do it]</char>? let him alone, and let him curse; for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has bidden him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />It may be that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will look on my affliction, and that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will requite <char style="pn">(repay)</char> me good for his cursing this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And as David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and his men went by the way, Shime’i <char style="add">[Fame]</char> went along on the hill’s side over against him, and cursed as he went, and threw stones at him, and cast dust.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And the king, and all the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him, came weary, and refreshed themselves there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>, and all the people the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, came to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and Achitofel <char style="add">[my brother i foolish]</char> with him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And it came to pass, when Hushai <char style="add">[hasting]</char> the Arki <char style="add">[lengthy]</char>, David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s friend, was come unto Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>, that Hushai <char style="add">[hasting]</char> said unto Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>, Long live the king! Long live the king!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> said to Hushai <char style="add">[hasting]</char>, <char style="add">[Is]</char> this you<char style="ord">i</char> kindness to you<char style="ord">i</char> friend? why went you<char style="ord">i</char> not with you<char style="ord">i</char> friend?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And Hushai <char style="add">[hasting]</char> said unto Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>, No; but whom the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and this people, and all the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, choose, his will I be, and with him will I abide.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And again, whom should I serve? <char style="add">[should I]</char> not <char style="add">[serve]</char> in the presence of his son? as I have served in you<char style="ord">i</char> father’s presence, so will I be in you<char style="ord">i</char> presence.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Then said Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> to Achitofel <char style="add">[my brother i foolish]</char>, Give counsel among you what we shall do.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Achitofel <char style="add">[my brother i foolish]</char> said unto Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>, Go in unto you<char style="ord">i</char> father’s concubines, which he has left to keep the house; and all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> shall hear that you<char style="ord">i</char> are abhorred of you<char style="ord">i</char> father: then shall the hands of all that <char style="add">[are]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char> be strong.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />So they spread Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> a tent upon the top of the house; and Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> went in unto his father’s concubines in the sight of all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And the counsel of Achitofel <char style="add">[my brother i foolish]</char>, which he counseled in those days, <char style="add">[was]</char> as if a man had enquired at the oracle of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>: so <char style="add">[was]</char> all the counsel of Achitofel <char style="add">[my brother i foolish]</char> both with David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and with Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="17" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Moreover Achitofel <char style="add">[my brother i foolish]</char> said unto Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>, Let me now choose out twelve thousand men, and I will arise and pursue after David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> this night:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And I will come upon him while he <char style="add">[is]</char> weary and weak handed, and will make him afraid: and all the people that <char style="add">[are]</char> with him shall flee; and I will strike the king only:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And I will bring back all the people unto you<char style="ord">i</char>: the man whom you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> as if all returned: <char style="add">[so]</char> all the people shall be in peace.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the saying pleased Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> well, and all the elders of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Then said Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>, Call now Hushai <char style="add">[hasting]</char> the Arki <char style="add">[lengthy]</char> also, and let us hear likewise what he says.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And when Hushai <char style="add">[hasting]</char> was come to Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>, Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> spoke unto him, saying, Achitofel <char style="add">[my brother i foolish]</char> has spoken after this manner: shall we do <char style="add">[after]</char> his saying? if not; speak you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Hushai <char style="add">[hasting]</char> said unto Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>, The counsel that Achitofel <char style="add">[my brother i foolish]</char> has given <char style="add">[is]</char> not good at this time.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />For, said Hushai <char style="add">[hasting]</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> know your<char style="ord">i</char> father and his men, that they <char style="add">[be]</char> mighty men, and they <char style="add">[be]</char> chafed in their minds, as a bear robbed of her whelps in the field: and your<char style="ord">i</char> father <char style="add">[is]</char> a man of war, and will not lodge with the people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Behold, he is hid now in some pit, or in some <char style="add">[other]</char> place: and it will come to pass, when some of them be overthrown at the first, that whosoever hears it will say, There is a slaughter among the people that follow Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And he also <char style="add">[that is]</char> valiant, whose heart <char style="add">[is]</char> as the heart of a lion, shall utterly melt: for all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> knows that you<char style="ord">i</char> father <char style="add">[is]</char> a mighty man, and <char style="add">[they]</char> which <char style="add">[be]</char> with him <char style="add">[are]</char> valiant men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Therefore I counsel that all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> be generally gathered unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, from Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char> even to Be’er-sheva <char style="add">[Well of the sevenfold Oath]</char>, as the sand that <char style="add">[is]</char> by the sea for multitude; and that you<char style="ord">i</char> go to battle in your<char style="ord">i</char> own person.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />So shall we come upon him in some place where he shall be found, and we will light upon him as the dew falls on the ground: and of him and of all the men that <char style="add">[are]</char> with him there shall not be left so much as one.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Moreover, if he be gotten into a city, then shall all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> bring ropes to that city, and we will draw it into the river, until there be not one small stone found there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> and all the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said, The counsel of Hushai <char style="add">[hasting]</char> the Arki <char style="add">[lengthy] [is]</char> better than the counsel of Achitofel <char style="add">[my brother i foolish]</char>. For the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had appointed to defeat the good counsel of Achitofel <char style="add">[my brother i foolish]</char>, to the intent that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> might bring evil upon Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Then said Hushai <char style="add">[hasting]</char> unto Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> and to Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great]</char> the priests, Thus and thus did Achitofel <char style="add">[my brother i foolish]</char> counsel Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> and the elders of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and thus and thus have I counseled.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Now therefore send quickly, and tell David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, saying, Lodge not this night in the plains of the wilderness, but speedily pass over; lest the king be swallow <char style="pn">(to approve, commend, accept)</char>ed up, and all the people that <char style="add">[are]</char> with him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Now Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> and Achima’atz <char style="add">[my brother is anger (wrath)]</char> detained <char style="pn">(held)</char> by ‘Ein-Rogel <char style="pn">(a place near Jerusalem)</char> <char style="add">[Fount of the Fuller (washer and/or bleacher of clothes)]</char>; for they might not be seen to come into the city: and a wench went and told them; and they went and told king David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Nevertheless a boy saw them, and told Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>: but they went both of them away quickly, and came to a man’s house in Bachurim <char style="add">[young men’s village]</char>, which had a well in his court; to which they went down.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the woman took and spread a covering over the well’s mouth, and spread ground corn thereon; and the thing was not known.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And when Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>’s servants came to the woman to the house, they said, Where <char style="add">[is]</char> Achima’atz <char style="add">[my brother is anger (wrath)]</char> and Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>? And the woman said unto them, They be gone over the brook of water. And when they had sought and could not find <char style="add">[them]</char>, they returned to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And it came to pass, after they were departed, that they came up out of the well, and went and told king David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and said unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, Arise, and pass quickly over the water: for thus has Achitofel <char style="add">[my brother i foolish]</char> counseled against you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Then David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> arose, and all the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him, and they passed over Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>: by the morning light there lacked not one of them that was not gone over Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And when Achitofel <char style="add">[my brother i foolish]</char> saw that his counsel was not followed, he saddled <char style="add">[his]</char> ass, and arose, and got him home to his house, to his city, and put his household in order, and hanged himself, and died, and was buried in the sepulcher of his father.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Then David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> came to Machanayim <char style="add">[Two Camps]</char>. And Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> passed over Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>, he and all the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> with him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> made ‘Amasa <char style="add">[burden]</char> captain of the host instead of Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>: which ‘Amasa <char style="add">[burden] [was]</char> a man’s son, whose name <char style="add">[was]</char> Yitra <char style="add">[abundance]</char> an Israeli, that went in to Avigayil <char style="add">[my father is joy]</char> the daughter of Nachash <char style="add">[serpent]</char>, sister to Tz’ruyah <char style="add">[balsam]</char> Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>’s mother.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />So Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> pitched in the land of Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And it came to pass, when David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> was come to Machanayim <char style="add">[Two Camps]</char>, that Shovi <char style="add">[glorious]</char> the son of Nachash <char style="add">[serpent]</char> of Rabbah <char style="add">[Great]</char> of the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, and Makhir <char style="add">[Sold]</char> the son of ‘Ammi’el <char style="add">[my kinsman is God] [My Kinsman is God]</char> of Lo-D’var <char style="add">[not a pasture]</char>, and Barzillai <char style="add">[my iron]</char> the Gil’adi <char style="add">[Hill of Testimony]</char> of Rogelim <char style="add">[place of fullers]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Brought beds, and basons, and earthen vessels, and wheat, and barley, and flour, and parched <char style="add">[corn]</char>, and beans, and lentiles, and parched <char style="add">[pulse (peas; beans; legumes)]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And honey, and butter, and sheep, and cheese of cattle, for David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and for the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him, to eat: for they said, The people <char style="add">[is]</char> hungry, and weary, and thirsty, in the wilderness.</para>
  <chapter number="18" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> numbered the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him, and set captains of thousands and captains of hundreds over them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> sent forth a third part of the people under the hand of Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, and a third part under the hand of Avishai <char style="add">[my father is a gift]</char> the son of Tz’ruyah <char style="add">[balsam]</char>, Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>’s brother, and a third part under the hand of Ittai <char style="add">[with me]</char> the Gitti <char style="add">[belonging to Gat (winepress)]</char>. And the king said unto the people, I will surely go forth with you myself also.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />But the people answered, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not go forth: for if we flee away, they will not care for us; neither if half of us die, will they care for us: but now <char style="add">[you<char style="ord">i</char> are]</char> worth ten thousand of us: therefore now <char style="add">[it is]</char> better that you<char style="ord">i</char> help <char style="pn">(aid)</char> us out of the city.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the king said unto them, What seems you best I will do. And the king stood by the gate side, and all the people came out by hundreds and by thousands.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the king commanded Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> and Avishai <char style="add">[my father is a gift]</char> and Ittai <char style="add">[with me]</char>, saying, <char style="add">[Deal]</char> gently for my sake with the young man, <char style="add">[even]</char> with Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>. And all the people heard when the king gave all the captains charge concerning Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />So the people went out into the field against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and the battle was in the wood of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Where the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> were slain before the servants of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and there was there a great slaughter that day of twenty thousand <char style="add">[men]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />For the battle was there scattered over the face of all the country: and the wood devoured more people that day than the sword devoured.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> met the servants of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>. And Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> rode upon a mule, and the mule went under the thick boughs of a great oak, and his head caught hold of the oak, and he was taken up between the heaven and the earth; and the mule that <char style="add">[was]</char> under him went away.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And a certain man saw <char style="add">[it]</char>, and told Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, and said, Behold, I saw Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> hanged in an oak.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> said unto the man that told him, And, behold, you<char style="ord">i</char> saw <char style="add">[him]</char>, and why did you<char style="ord">i</char> not strike him there to the ground? and I would have given you<char style="ord">i</char> ten <char style="add">[shekels]</char> of silver, and a belt.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the man said unto Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, Though I should receive a thousand <char style="add">[shekels]</char> of silver in my hand, <char style="add">[yet]</char> would I not put forth my hand against the king’s son: for in our hearing the king charged you<char style="ord">i</char> and Avishai <char style="add">[my father is a gift]</char> and Ittai <char style="add">[with me]</char>, saying, Beware that none <char style="add">[touch]</char> the young man Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Otherwise I should have wrought falsehood against my own life: for there is no matter hid from the king, and you<char style="ord">i</char> yourself would have set yourself against <char style="add">[me]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Then said Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, I may not wait thus with you<char style="ord">i</char>. And he took three darts in his hand, and thrust them through the heart of Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>, while he <char style="add">[was]</char> yet alive in the midst of the oak.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And ten young men that bore Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>’s armour compassed about and struck Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>, and killed him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> blew the trumpet, and the people returned from pursuing after Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: for Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> held back the people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And they took Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>, and cast him into a great pit in the wood, and laid a very great heap of stones upon him: and all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> fled everyone to his tent.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Now Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> in his lifetime had taken and reared up for himself a pillar, which <char style="add">[is]</char> in the king’s dale: for he said, I have no son to keep my name in remembrance: and he called the pillar after his own name: and it is called unto this day, Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>’s place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Then said Achima’atz [my brother is anger (wrath)] the son of Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char>, Let me now run, and bear the king tidings, how that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has avenged him of his enemies.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> said unto him, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not bear tidings this day, but you<char style="ord">i</char> shall bear tidings another day: but this day you<char style="ord">i</char> shall bear no tidings, because the king’s son is dead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Then said Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> to Kushi <char style="add">[their blackness]</char>, Go tell the king what you<char style="ord">i</char> have seen. And Kushi <char style="add">[their blackness]</char> bowed himself unto Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, and ran.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Then said Achima’atz <char style="add">[my brother is anger (wrath)]</char> the son of Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> yet again to Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, But howsoever, let me, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, also run after Kushi <char style="add">[their blackness]</char>. And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> said, For what reason will you<char style="ord">i</char> run, my son, seeing that you<char style="ord">i</char> have no tidings ready?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />But howsoever, <char style="add">[said he]</char>, let me run. And he said unto him, Run. Then Achima’atz <char style="add">[my brother is anger (wrath)]</char> ran by the way of the plain, and overran Kushi <char style="add">[their blackness]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> sat between the two gates: and the watchman went up to the roof over the gate unto the wall, and lifted up his eyes, and looked, and behold a man running alone.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And the watchman cried, and told the king. And the king said, If he <char style="add">[be]</char> alone, <char style="add">[there is]</char> tidings in his mouth. And he came apace <char style="pn">(at a quick pace; quickly)</char>, and drew near.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And the watchman saw another man running: and the watchman called unto the porter, and said, Behold <char style="add">[another]</char> man running alone. And the king said, He also brings tidings.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And the watchman said, I think the running of the foremost is like the running of Achima’atz <char style="add">[my brother is anger (wrath)]</char> the son of Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char>. And the king said, He <char style="add">[is]</char> a good man, and comes with good tidings.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And Achima’atz <char style="add">[my brother is anger (wrath)]</char> called, and said unto the king, All is well. And he fell down to the earth upon his face before the king, and said, Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, which has delivered up the men that lifted up their hand against my lord the king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And the king said, Is the young man Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> safe? And Achima’atz <char style="add">[my brother is anger (wrath)]</char> answered, When Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> sent the king’s servant, and <char style="add">[me]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> servant, I saw a great tumult, but I knew not what <char style="add">[it was]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And the king said <char style="add">[unto him]</char>, Turn aside, <char style="add">[and]</char> stand here. And he turned aside, and stood still.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And, behold, Kushi <char style="add">[their blackness]</char> came; and Kushi <char style="add">[their blackness]</char> said, Tidings, my lord the king: for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has avenged you<char style="ord">i</char> this day of all them that rose up against you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And the king said unto Kushi <char style="add">[their blackness]</char>, Is the young man Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> safe? And Kushi <char style="add">[their blackness]</char> answered, The enemies of my lord the king, and all that rise against you<char style="ord">i</char> to do <char style="pn">[you<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> hurt, be as <char style="add">[that]</char> young man <char style="add">[is]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And the king was much moved, and went up to the chamber over the gate, and wept: and as he went, thus he said, O my son Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>, my son, my son Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>! would God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> I had died for you<char style="ord">i</char>, O Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>, my son, my son!</para>
  <chapter number="19" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it was told Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, Behold, the king weep and mourns for Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the victory that day was <char style="add">[turned]</char> into mourning unto all the people: for the people heard say that day how the king was grieved for his son.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the people got them by stealth that day into the city, as people being ashamed steal away when they flee in battle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />But the king covered his face, and the king cried with a loud voice, O my son Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>, O Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>, my son, my son!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> came into the house to the king, and said, you<char style="ord">i</char> have shamed this day the faces of all you<char style="ord">i</char> servants, which this day have saved your<char style="ord">i</char> life, and the lives of your<char style="ord">i</char> sons and of your<char style="ord">i</char> daughters, and the lives of your<char style="ord">i</char> wives, and the lives of your<char style="ord">i</char> concubines;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />In that you<char style="ord">i</char> love your<char style="ord">i</char> enemies, and hate your<char style="ord">i</char> friends. For you<char style="ord">i</char> have declared this day, that you<char style="ord">i</char> regard neither princes nor servants: for this day I perceive, that if Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> had lived, and all we had died this day, then it had pleased you<char style="ord">i</char> well.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Now therefore arise, go forth, and speak comfortably unto you<char style="ord">i</char> servants: for I swear by the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, if you<char style="ord">i</char> go not forth, there will not wait one with you<char style="ord">i</char> this night: and that will be worse unto you<char style="ord">i</char> than all the evil that befell you<char style="ord">i</char> from you<char style="ord">i</char> youth until now.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Then the king arose, and sat in the gate. And they told unto all the people, saying, Behold, the king does sit in the gate. And all the people came before the king: for Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> had fled every man to his tent.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And all the people were at strife throughout all the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, saying, The king saved us out of the hand of our enemies, and he delivered us out of the hand of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>; and now he is fled out of the land for Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>, whom we anointed over us, is dead in battle. Now therefore why speak you<char style="ord">2f</char> not a word of bringing the king back?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And king David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> sent to Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> and to Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great]</char> the priests, saying, Speak unto the elders of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, saying, Why are you<char style="ord">2f</char> the last to bring the king back to his house? seeing the speech of all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> is come to the king, <char style="add">[even]</char> to his house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> my brethren, you<char style="ord">2f</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> my bones and my flesh: wherefore then are you<char style="ord">2f</char> the last to bring back the king?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And say you<char style="ord">2f</char> to ‘Amasa <char style="add">[burden]</char>, <char style="add">[Are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> not of my bone, and of my flesh? God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> do so to me, and more also, if you<char style="ord">i</char> be not captain of the host before me continually in the room of Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And he bowed the heart of all the men of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, even as <char style="add">[the heart of]</char> one man; so that they sent <char style="add">[this word]</char> unto the king, Return you<char style="ord">i</char>, and all you<char style="ord">i</char> servants.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />So the king returned, and came to Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>. And Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> came to Gilgal <char style="add">[A Wheel, Rolling]</char>, to go to meet the king, to conduct the king over Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And Shime’i <char style="add">[Fame]</char> the son of Gera <char style="add">[A Grain]</char>, from the tribe of Binyamin <char style="add">[A Son of the Right Hand]</char>, which <char style="add">[was]</char> of Bachurim <char style="add">[young men’s village]</char>, hasted and came down with the men of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> to meet king David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And <char style="add">[there were]</char> a thousand men of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> with him, and Tziva <char style="add">[statue]</char> the servant of the house of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, and his fifteen sons and his twenty servants with him; and they went over Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char> before the king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And there went over a ferry boat to carry over the king’s household, and to do what he thought good. And Shime’i <char style="add">[Fame]</char> the son of Gera <char style="add">[A Grain]</char> fell down before the king, as he was come over Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And said unto the king, Let not my lord impiute <char style="pn">(charge to one’s account; reckon)</char> iniquity unto me, neither do you<char style="ord">i</char> remember that which you<char style="ord">i</char> servant did perversely the day that my lord the king went out of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, that the king should take it to his heart.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />For you<char style="ord">i</char> servant does know that I have sinned: therefore, behold, I am come the first this day of all the house of Yosef [<char style="pn">(God)</char> He Shall Add] to go down to meet my lord the king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />But Avishai <char style="add">[my father is a gift]</char> the son of Tz’ruyah <char style="add">[balsam]</char> answered and said, Shall not Shime’i <char style="add">[Fame]</char> be put to death for this, because he cursed the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> anointed?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said, What have I to do with you, you<char style="ord">2f</char> sons of Tz’ruyah <char style="add">[balsam]</char>, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> should this day be adversaries unto me? shall there any man be put to death this day in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>? for do not I know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> this day king over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Therefore the king said unto Shime’i <char style="add">[Fame]</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not die. And the king swore unto him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And M’fivoshet <char style="add">[exterminating the idol]</char> the son of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> came down to meet the king, and had neither dressed his feet, nor trimmed his beard, nor washed his clothes, from the day the king departed until the day he came <char style="add">[again]</char> in peace.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And it came to pass, when he was come to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> to meet the king, that the king said unto him, For what reason went not you<char style="ord">i</char> with me, M’fivoshet <char style="add">[exterminating the idol]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And he answered, My lord, O king, my servant deceived me: for you<char style="ord">i</char> servant said, I will saddle me an ass, that I may ride thereon, and go to the king; because you<char style="ord">i</char> servant <char style="add">[is]</char> lame.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And he has slandered you<char style="ord">i</char> servant unto my lord the king; but my lord the king <char style="add">[is]</char> as an angel of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>: do therefore <char style="add">[what is]</char> good in you<char style="ord">i</char> eyes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />For all <char style="add">[of]</char> my father’s house were but dead men before my lord the king: yet did you<char style="ord">i</char> set you<char style="ord">i</char> servant among them that did eat at you<char style="ord">i</char> own table. What right therefore have I yet to cry any more unto the king?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And the king said unto him, Why speak you<char style="ord">i</char> any more of you<char style="ord">i</char> matters? I have said, you<char style="ord">i</char> and Tziva <char style="add">[statue]</char> divide the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And M’fivoshet <char style="add">[exterminating the idol]</char> said unto the king, Yes, let him take all, forasmuch as my lord the king is come again in peace unto his own house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And Barzillai <char style="add">[my iron]</char> the Gil’adi <char style="add">[Hill of Testimony]</char> came down from Rogelim <char style="add">[place of fullers]</char>, and went over Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char> with the king, to conduct him over Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />Now Barzillai <char style="add">[my iron]</char> was a very aged man, <char style="add">[even]</char> eighty years old: and he had provided the king of sustenance while he lay at Machanayim <char style="add">[Two Camps]</char>; for he <char style="add">[was]</char> a very great man.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And the king said unto Barzillai <char style="add">[my iron]</char>, Come you<char style="ord">i</char> over with me, and I will feed you<char style="ord">i</char> with me in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And Barzillai <char style="add">[my iron]</char> said unto the king, How long have I to live, that I should go up with the king unto Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />I <char style="add">[am]</char> this day eighty years old: <char style="add">[and]</char> can I discern between good and evil? can you<char style="ord">i</char> servant taste what I eat or what I drink? can I hear any more the voice of singing men and singing women? wherefore then should your<char style="ord">i</char> servant be yet a burden unto my lord the king?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />You<char style="ord">1s</char> servant will go a little way over Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char> with the king: and why should the king recompense it me with such a reward?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />Let your<char style="ord">i</char> servant, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, turn back again, that I may die in my own city, <char style="add">[and be buried]</char> by the grave of my father and of my mother. But behold your<char style="ord">i</char> servant Khimham <char style="add">[their longing]</char>; let him go over with my lord the king; and do to him what shall seem good unto you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And the king answered, Khimham <char style="add">[their longing]</char> shall go over with me, and I will do to him that which shall seem good unto you<char style="ord">i</char>: and whatsoever you<char style="ord">i</char> shall require of me, <char style="add">[that]</char> will I do for you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />And all the people went over Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>. And when the king was come over, the king kissed Barzillai <char style="add">[my iron]</char>, and Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> him; and he returned unto his own place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />Then the king went on to Gilgal <char style="add">[A Wheel, Rolling]</char>, and Khimham <char style="add">[their longing]</char> went on with him: and all the people of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> conducted the king, and also half the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />And, behold, all the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> came to the king, and said unto the king, Why have our brethren the men of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> stolen you<char style="ord">i</char> away, and have brought the king, and his household, and all David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s men with him, over Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />And all the men of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> answered the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Because the king <char style="add">[is]</char> near of family to us: wherefore then be you<char style="ord">2f</char> angry for this matter? have we eaten at all of the king’s <char style="add">[cost]</char>? or has he given us any gift?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />And the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> answered the men of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and said, We have ten parts in the king, and we have also more <char style="add">[right]</char> in David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> than you<char style="ord">2f</char>: why then did you<char style="ord">2f</char> despise us, that our advice should not be first had in bringing back our king? And the words of the men of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> were fiercer than the words of the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="20" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And there happened to be there a man of Belial <char style="add">[Worthless, Good for Nothing]</char>, whose name <char style="add">[was]</char> Sheva <char style="add">[Seven]</char>, the son of Bikhri <char style="add">[youthful]</char>, from the tribe of Binyamin <char style="add">[A Son of the Right Hand]</char>: and he blew a trumpet, and said, We have no part in David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, neither have we inheritance in the son of Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char>: every man to his tents, O Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />So every man of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went up from after David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> followed Sheva <char style="add">[Seven]</char> the son of Bikhri <char style="add">[youthful]</char>: but the men of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> clave unto their king, from Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char> even to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> came to his house at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>; and the king took the ten women <char style="add">[his]</char> concubines, whom he had left to keep the house, and put them in ward (in custody, with a guard; prison), and fed them, but went not in unto them. So they were shut up unto the day of their death, living in widowhood.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Then said the king to ‘Amasa <char style="add">[burden]</char>, Assemble me the men of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> within three days, and be you<char style="ord">i</char> here present.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />So ‘Amasa <char style="add">[burden]</char> went to assemble <char style="add">[the men of]</char> Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>: but he tarried longer than the set time which he had appointed him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said to Avishai <char style="add">[my father is a gift]</char>, Now shall Sheva <char style="add">[Seven]</char> the son of Bikhri <char style="add">[youthful]</char> do us more harm than <char style="add">[did]</char> Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>: take you<char style="ord">i</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> lord’s servants, and pursue after him, lest he get him fenced cities, and escape us.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And there went out after him Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>’s men, and the K’reti <char style="add">[executioners]</char>, and the P’leti <char style="add">[couriers]</char>, and all the mighty men: and they went out of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, to pursue after Sheva <char style="add">[Seven]</char> the son of Bikhri <char style="add">[youthful]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />When they <char style="add">[were]</char> at the great stone which <char style="add">[is]</char> in Giv’on <char style="add">[Hill City]</char>, ‘Amasa <char style="add">[burden]</char> went before them. And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>’s garment that he had put on was girded unto him, and upon it a belt <char style="add">[with]</char> a sword fastened upon his waist in the sheath thereof; and as he went forth it fell out.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> said to ‘Amasa <char style="add">[burden]</char>, <char style="add">[Are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> in health, my brother? And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> took ‘Amasa <char style="add">[burden]</char> by the beard with the right hand to kiss him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />But ‘Amasa <char style="add">[burden]</char> took no heed to the sword that <char style="add">[was]</char> in Yo’av’s <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>’s hand: so he struck him with that in the fifth <char style="add">[rib]</char>, and shed out his bowels <char style="pn">(inward parts; affections)</char> to the ground, and struck him not again; and he died. So Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> and Avishai <char style="add">[my father is a gift]</char> his brother pursued after Sheva <char style="add">[Seven]</char> the son of Bikhri <char style="add">[youthful]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And one of Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>’s men stood by him, and said, He that favours Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, and he that <char style="add">[is]</char> for David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, <char style="add">[let him go]</char> after Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And ‘Amasa <char style="add">[burden]</char> wallow <char style="pn">(to approve, commend, accept)</char>ed in blood in the midst of the highway. And when the man saw that all the people stood still, he removed ‘Amasa <char style="add">[burden]</char> out of the highway into the field, and cast a cloth upon him, when he saw that everyone that came by him stood still.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />When he was removed out of the highway, all the people went on after Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, to pursue after Sheva <char style="add">[Seven]</char> the son of Bikhri <char style="add">[youthful]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And he went through all the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> unto Hevel <char style="pn">(herdsman)</char>, and to Beit-Ma’akhah <char style="add">[oppression] [house of pressure]</char>, and all the Berim <char style="add">[my well; of the well]</char>: and they were gathered together, and went also after him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And they came and besieged him in Hevel <char style="pn">(herdsman)</char> of Beit-Ma’akhah <char style="add">[oppression] [house of pressure]</char>, and they cast up a bank against the city, and it stood in the trench: and all the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> with Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> battered the wall, to throw it down.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Then cried a wise woman out of the city, Hear, hear; say, I pray you, unto Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, Come near here, that I may speak with you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And when he was come near unto her, the woman said, <char style="add">[Are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>? And he answered, I <char style="add">[am he]</char>. Then she said unto him, Hear the words of your<char style="ord">i</char> female servant. And he answered, I do hear.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Then she spoke, saying, They were wont <char style="pn">(used to; in the habit of)</char> to speak in old time, saying, They shall surely ask <char style="add">[counsel]</char> at Hevel <char style="pn">(herdsman)</char>: and so they ended <char style="add">[the matter]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />I <char style="add">[am one of them that are]</char> peaceable <char style="add">[and]</char> faithful in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: you<char style="ord">i</char> seek to destroy a city and a mother in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: why will you<char style="ord">i</char> swallow <char style="pn">(to approve, commend, accept)</char> up the inheritance of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> answered and said, Far be it, far be it from me, that I should swallow <char style="pn">(to approve, commend, accept)</char> up or destroy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />The matter <char style="add">[is]</char> not so: but a man of mount Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, Sheva <char style="add">[Seven]</char> the son of Bikhri <char style="add">[youthful]</char> by name, has lifted up his hand against the king, <char style="add">[even]</char> against David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>: deliver him only, and I will depart from the city. And the woman said unto Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, Behold, his head shall be thrown to you<char style="ord">i</char> over the wall.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Then the woman went unto all the people in her wisdom. And they cut off the head of Sheva <char style="add">[Seven]</char> the son of Bikhri <char style="add">[youthful]</char>, and cast <char style="add">[it]</char> out to Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>. And he blew a trumpet, and they retired from the city, every man to his tent. And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> returned to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> unto the king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Now Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father] [was]</char> over all the host of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and B’nayahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has built]</char> the son of Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows] [was]</char> over the K’reti <char style="add">[executioners]</char> and over the P’leti <char style="add">[couriers]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And Adoram <char style="add">[my lord is exalted] [was]</char> over the tribute: and Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> the son of Achilud <char style="add">[child’s brother] [was]</char> recorder:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And Sheva <char style="add">[was]</char> scribe: and Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> and Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great] [were]</char> the priests:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And ‘Ira <char style="add">[watchful of a city]</char> also the Ya’iri <char style="add">[descendant of Ya’ir (He Will Enlighten)]</char> was a chief ruler about David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="21" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then there was a famine in the days of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> three years, year after year; and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> enquired of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> answered, <char style="add">[It is]</char> for Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, and for <char style="add">[his]</char> bloody house, because he killed the Giv’onim <char style="add">[little hill; hilly]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the king called the Giv’onim <char style="add">[little hill; hilly]</char>, and said unto them; (now the Giv’onim <char style="add">[little hill; hilly] [were]</char> not of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, but of the remnant of the Emori <char style="add">[Highlanders]</char>; and the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> had sworn unto them: and Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> sought to slay them in his zeal to the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />For what reason David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto the Giv’onim <char style="add">[little hill; hilly]</char>, What shall I do for you? and which shall I make the atonement, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> may bless the inheritance of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the Giv’onim <char style="add">[little hill; hilly]</char> said unto him, We will have no silver nor gold of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, nor of his house; neither for us shall you<char style="ord">i</char> kill any man in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>. And he said, What you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall say, <char style="add">[that]</char> will I do for you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And they answered the king, The man that consumed us, and that devised against us <char style="add">[that]</char> we should be destroyed from remaining in any of the coasts of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Let seven men of his sons be delivered unto us, and we will hang them up unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char> of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, <char style="add">[whom]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> did choose. And the king said, I will give <char style="add">[them]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />But the king spared M’fivoshet <char style="add">[exterminating the idol]</char>, the son of Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> the son of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, because of the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> oath that <char style="add">[was]</char> between them, between David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> the son of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />But the king took the two sons of Ritzpah <char style="add">[pavement]</char> the daughter of Ayah <char style="add">[falcon]</char>, whom she bore unto Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, Armoni <char style="add">[one of the palace]</char> and M’fivoshet <char style="add">[exterminating the idol]</char>; and the five sons of Mikhal <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> the daughter of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, whom she brought up for Adri’el <char style="add">[flock of God]</char> the son of Barzillai <char style="add">[my iron]</char> the Mecholati <char style="add">[dancing (in sadness)]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And he delivered them into the hands of the Giv’onim <char style="add">[little hill; hilly]</char>, and they hanged them in the hill before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and they fell <char style="add">[all]</char> seven together, and were put to death in the days of harvest, in the first <char style="add">[days]</char>, in the beginning of barley harvest.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Ritzpah <char style="add">[pavement]</char> the daughter of Ayah <char style="add">[falcon]</char> took sackcloth, and spread it for her upon the rock, from the beginning of harvest until water dropped upon them out of heaven, and suffered neither the birds of the air to rest on them by day, nor the beasts of the field by night.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And it was told David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> what Ritzpah <char style="add">[pavement]</char> the daughter of Ayah <char style="add">[falcon]</char>, the concubine of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, had done.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> went and took the bones of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and the bones of Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> his son from the men of Yavesh-Gil’ad <char style="add">[Dry Hill of Testimony]</char>, which had stolen them from the street of Beit-Sh’an <char style="add">[house of ease]</char>, where the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> had hanged them, when the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> had slain Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> in Gilboa <char style="add">[swollen heap]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And he brought up from there the bones of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and the bones of Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> his son; and they gathered the bones of them that were hanged.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And the bones of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> and Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> his son buried they in the country of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> in Tzela <char style="add">[a rib]</char>, in the sepulcher of Kish <char style="add">[bent]</char> his father: and they performed all that the king commanded. And after that God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> was entreated for the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Moreover the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> had yet war again with Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> went down, and his servants with him, and fought against the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>: and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> waxed faint.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And Yishbi-B’nov <char style="add">[his dwelling is in Nov (discourse; prophecy)]</char>, which <char style="add">[was]</char> of the sons of the giant, the weight of whose spear <char style="add">[weighed]</char> three hundred <char style="add">[shekels]</char> of brass in weight, he being girded with a new <char style="add">[sword]</char>, thought to have slain David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />But Avishai <char style="add">[my father is a gift]</char> the son of Tz’ruyah <char style="add">[balsam]</char> succored him, and struck the P’lishtim <char style="add">[immigrants]</char>, and killed him. Then the men of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> swore unto him, saying, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall go no more out with us to battle, that you<char style="ord">i</char> quench not the light of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And it came to pass after this, that there was again a battle with the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> at Gov <char style="add">[cistern]</char>: then Sibkhai <char style="add">[weaver]</char> the Hushati <char style="add">[meaning unknown]</char> killed Saf <char style="add">[tall]</char>, which <char style="add">[was]</char> of the sons of the giant.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And there was again a battle in Gov <char style="add">[cistern]</char> with the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, where Elchanan <char style="add">[God has been gracious]</char> the son of Ya’arei-Orgim <char style="add">[forests of weaver]</char>, a Beit-Lachmi <char style="add">[house of bread]</char>, killed <char style="add">[the brother of]</char> Golyat <char style="add">[splendor]</char> the Gitti <char style="add">[belonging to Gat (winepress)]</char>, the staff of whose spear <char style="add">[was]</char> like a weaver’s beam.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And there was yet a battle in Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char>, where was a man of <char style="add">[great]</char> stature, that had on every hand six fingers, and on every foot six toes, four and twenty in number; and he also was born to the giant.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And when he defied Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> the son of Shim’ah <char style="add">[fame]</char> the brother of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> killed him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />These four were born to the giant in Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char>, and fell by the hand of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and by the hand of his servants.</para>
  <chapter number="22" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> spoke unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> the words of this song in the day <char style="add">[that]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had delivered him out of the hand of all his enemies, and out of the hand of Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he said, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> my rock, and my fortress, and my deliverer;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />The God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of my rock; in him will I trust: <char style="add">[he is]</char> my shield, and the horn of my salvation, my high tower, and my refuge, my saviour; you<char style="ord">i</char> save me from violence.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />I will call on the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, <char style="add">[who is]</char> worthy to be praised: so shall I be saved from my enemies.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />When the waves of death compassed me, the floods of ungodly men made me afraid;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />The sorrows of hell compassed me about; the snares of death prevented me;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />In my distress I called upon the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and cried to my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>: and he did hear my voice out of his temple, and my cry <char style="add">[did enter]</char> into his ears.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Then the earth shook and trembled; the foundations of heaven moved and shook, because he was exceedingly angry.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />There went up a smoke out of his nostrils, and fire out of his mouth devoured: coals were kindled by it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />He bowed the heavens also, and came down; and darkness <char style="add">[was]</char> under his feet.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And he rode upon a cherub <char style="add">[keruv]</char>, and did fly: and he was seen upon the wings of the wind.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And he made darkness pavilions round about him, dark waters, <char style="add">[and]</char> thick clouds of the skies.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Through the brightness before him were coals of fire kindled.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> thundered from heaven, and the most High uttered his voice.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And he sent out arrows, and scattered them; lightning, and scattered <char style="pn">(defeated in battle)</char> them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And the channels of the sea appeared, the foundations of the world were discovered, at the rebuking of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, at the blast of the breath of his nostrils.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />He sent from above, he took me; he drew me out of many waters;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />He delivered me from my strong enemy, <char style="add">[and]</char> from them that hated me: for they were too strong for me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />They prevented me in the day of my calamity: but the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was my stay.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />He brought me forth also into a large place: he delivered me, because he delighted in me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> rewarded me according to my righteousness: according to the cleanness of my hands has he recompensed me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />For I have kept the ways of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and have not wickedly departed from my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />For all his judgments <char style="add">[were]</char> before me: and <char style="add">[as for]</char> his statutes, I did not depart from them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />I was also upright before him, and have kept myself from my iniquity.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Therefore the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has recompensed me according to my righteousness; according to my cleanness in his eye sight.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />With the merciful you<char style="ord">i</char> will show yourself merciful, <char style="add">[and]</char> with the upright man you<char style="ord">i</char> will show yourself upright.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />With the pure you<char style="ord">i</char> will show yourself pure; and with the perverse <char style="pn">(twisted)</char> <char style="add">[habitually disposed to disobedience and opposition]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> will show yourself unsavoury.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And the afflicted people you<char style="ord">i</char> will save: but your<char style="ord">i</char> eyes <char style="add">[are]</char> upon the arrogant <char style="pn">(proud; lifted up)</char>, <char style="add">[that]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> may bring <char style="add">[them]</char> down.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />For you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> my lamp, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will lighten my darkness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />For by you<char style="ord">i</char> I have run through a troop: by my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> have I leaped over a wall.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[As for]</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, his way <char style="add">[is]</char> perfect; the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> tried: he <char style="add">[is]</char> a buckler <char style="pn">(round shielf held with a grip)</char> to all them that trust in him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />For who <char style="add">[is]</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, save the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>? and who <char style="add">[is]</char> a rock, save our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered] [is]</char> my strength <char style="add">[and]</char> power: and he makes my way perfect.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />He makes my feet like hinds’ <char style="add">[feet]</char>: and sets me upon my high places.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />He teaches my hands to war; so that a bow of steel is broken by my arms.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> have also given me the shield of your<char style="ord">i</char> salvation: and your<char style="ord">i</char> gentleness has made me great.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> have enlarged my steps under me; so that my feet did not slip.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />I have pursued my enemies, and destroyed them; and turned not again until I had consumed them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />And I have consumed them, and wounded them, that they could not arise: yes, they are fallen under my feet.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />For you<char style="ord">i</char> have girded me with strength to battle: them that rose up against me have you<char style="ord">i</char> subdued under me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> have also given me the necks of my enemies, that I might destroy them that hate me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />They looked, but <char style="add">[there was]</char> none to save; <char style="add">[even]</char> unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, but he answered them not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />Then did I beat them as small as the dust of the earth, I did stamp them as the mire of the street, <char style="add">[and]</char> did spread them abroad.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> also have delivered me from the strivings of my people, you<char style="ord">i</char> have kept me <char style="add">[to be]</char> head of the heathen: a people <char style="add">[which]</char> I knew not shall serve me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" />Strangers shall submit themselves unto me: as soon as they hear, they shall be obedient unto me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" />Strangers shall fade away, and they shall be afraid out of their close places.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="47" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives; and Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> my rock; and exalted be the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of the rock of my salvation.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="48" style="v" />It <char style="add">[is]</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> that avenges me, and that brings down the people under me,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" />And that brings me forth from my enemies: you<char style="ord">i</char> also have lifted me up on high above them that rose up against me: you<char style="ord">i</char> have delivered me from the violent man.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="50" style="v" />Therefore I will give thanks unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, among the heathen, and I will sing praises unto your<char style="ord">i</char> name.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="51" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[He is]</char> the tower of salvation for his king: and shows mercy to his anointed, unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and to his seed forevermore.</para>
  <chapter number="23" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now these <char style="add">[be]</char> the last words of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>. David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> the son of Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char> said, and the man <char style="add">[who was]</char> raised up on high, the anointed of the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>, and the sweet psalmist of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, said,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />The Spirit of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke by me, and his word <char style="add">[was]</char> in my tongue.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />The God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said, the Rock of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> spoke to me, He that rules over men <char style="add">[must be]</char> just, ruling in the fear of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And <char style="add">[he shall be]</char> as the light of the morning, <char style="add">[when]</char> the sun rises, <char style="add">[even]</char> a morning without clouds; <char style="add">[as]</char> the tender grass <char style="add">[springing]</char> out of the earth by clear shining after rain.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Although my house <char style="add">[be]</char> not so with God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>; yet he has made with me an everlasting covenant, ordered in all <char style="add">[things]</char>, and sure: for <char style="add">[this is]</char> all my salvation, and all <char style="add">[my]</char> desire, although he make <char style="add">[it]</char> not to grow.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />But <char style="add">[the sons]</char> of Belial <char style="add">[Worthless, Good for Nothing] [shall be]</char> all of them as thorns thrust away, because they cannot be taken with hands:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />But the man <char style="add">[that]</char> shall to (to do entirely, do wholly) uch them must be fenced with iron and the staff of a spear; and they shall be utterly burned with fire in the <char style="add">[same]</char> place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />These <char style="add">[be]</char> the names of the mighty men whom David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> had: The Tach’kmoni <char style="add">[you will make me wise]</char> that sat in the seat, chief among the captains; the same <char style="add">[was]</char> ‘Adino <char style="add">[his ornament]</char> his ornament the ‘Etzni <char style="add">[sharp, strong, spear]</char>: <char style="add">[he lift up his spear]</char> against eight hundred, whom he killed at one time.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And after him <char style="add">[was]</char> El’azar <char style="add">[God has helped]</char> the son of Dodo <char style="add">[his beloved]</char> the Achochi <char style="add">[God prevails]</char>, <char style="add">[one]</char> of the three mighty men with David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, when they defied the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants] [that]</char> were there gathered together to battle, and the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> were gone away:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />He arose, and struck the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> until his hand was weary, and his hand clave unto the sword: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> wrought a great victory that day; and the people returned after him only to spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And after him <char style="add">[was]</char> Shammah <char style="add">[astonishment]</char> the son of Age <char style="add">[I shall increase]</char> the Harari <char style="add">[mountain dweller]</char>. And the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> were gathered together into a troop, where was a piece of ground full of lentiles: and the people fled from the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />But he stood in the midst of the ground, and defended it, and killed the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> wrought a great victory.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And three of the thirty chief went down, and came to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> in the harvest time unto the cave of ‘Adulam <char style="add">[Justice of the People]</char>: and the troop of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> pitched in the valley of Refa’im <char style="add">[giants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved] [was]</char> then in an hold, and the Garrison <char style="pn">(fortification; military post)</char> of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants] [was]</char> then <char style="add">[in]</char> Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> longed, and said, Oh that one would give me drink of the water of the well of Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> by the gate!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And the three mighty men broke through the host of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and drew water out of the well of Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char>, that <char style="add">[was]</char> by the gate, and took <char style="add">[it]</char>, and brought <char style="add">[it]</char> to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>: nevertheless he would not drink thereof, but poured it out unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And he said, Be it far from me, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, that I should do this: <char style="add">[is not this]</char> the blood of the men that went in jeopardy of their lives? therefore he would not drink it. These things did these three mighty men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And Avishai <char style="add">[my father is a gift]</char>, the brother of Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, the son of Tz’ruyah <char style="add">[balsam]</char>, was chief among three. And he lifted up his spear against three hundred, <char style="add">[and]</char> killed <char style="add">[them]</char>, and had the name among three.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Was he not most honourable of three? therefore he was their captain: howbeit he attained not unto the <char style="add">[first]</char> three.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And B’nayahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has built]</char> the son of Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char>, the son of a valiant man, of Kavtze’el <char style="add">[God Gathers]</char>, who had done many acts, he killed two lionlike men of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>: he went down also and killed a lion in the midst of a pit in time of snow:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And he killed an Mitzri <char style="add">[Egyptian]</char>, a goodly man: and the Mitzri <char style="add">[Egyptian]</char> had a spear in his hand; but he went down to him with a staff, and plucked the spear out of the Mitzri <char style="add">[Egyptian]</char>’s hand, and killed him with his own spear.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />These <char style="add">[things]</char> did B’nayahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has built]</char> the son of Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char>, and had the name among three mighty men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />He was more honourable than the thirty, but he attained not to the <char style="add">[first]</char> three. And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> set him over his guard.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />‘Asah’el <char style="add">[God-made]</char> the brother of Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father] [was]</char> one of the thirty; Elchanan <char style="add">[God has been gracious]</char> the son of Dodo <char style="add">[his beloved]</char> of Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Shammah <char style="add">[astonishment]</char> the Harodi <char style="add">[trembling]</char>, Elika <char style="add">[my God rejects]</char> the Harodi <char style="add">[trembling]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Heletz <char style="add">[he has saved]</char> the Palti <char style="add">[escape]</char>, ‘Ira <char style="add">[watchful of a city]</char> the son of ‘Ikesh <char style="add">[twisted]</char> the T’koai <char style="add">[trumpet blast]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Avi-ezer <char style="add">[My Father is Help]</char> the ‘Anatot <char style="add">[affliction]</char>, M’vunai <char style="add">[building of Yehovah]</char> the Hushati <char style="add">[meaning unknown]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Tzalmon <char style="add">[shady]</char> the Achochi <char style="add">[God prevails]</char>, Mahrai <char style="add">[impetuous]</char> the N’tofati <char style="add">[dropping]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />Helev <char style="add">[milk]</char> the son of Ba’anah <char style="add">[in affliction]</char>, a N’tofati <char style="add">[dropping]</char>, Ittai <char style="add">[with me]</char> the son of Rivai <char style="add">[pleader with Yehovah]</char> out of Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char> of the children of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />B’nayahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has built]</char> the Pir’atoni <char style="add">[Princely]</char>, Hiddai <char style="add">[for the rejoicing of Yehovah]</char> of the brooks of Ga’ash <char style="add">[Quaking]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />Avi-’Alvon [El <char style="pn">(God)</char> is my father] the ‘Arati <char style="add">[desert house]</char>, ‘Azmavet <char style="add">[strong unto death]</char> the Barchumi [son of the blackened: in the pitied],</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />Elyachba <char style="add">[God hides]</char> the Sha’alvoni <char style="add">[place of foxes]</char>, of the sons of Yashen <char style="add">[sleeping]</char>, Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />Shammah <char style="add">[astonishment]</char> the Harari <char style="add">[mountain dweller]</char>, Achi’am [mother’s brother] the son of Sharar <char style="add">[enemy]</char> the Harari <char style="add">[mountain dweller]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />Elifelet <char style="add">[God is deliverance]</char> the son of Achasbai <char style="add">[brother of my encompassers]</char>, the son of the Ma’akhati <char style="add">[pressure (literally, she has pressed)]</char>, Eli’am <char style="add">[God of the people, or God is kinsman]</char> the son of Achitofel <char style="add">[my brother i foolish]</char> the Giloni <char style="add">[gentilic of preceding]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />Hetzrai <char style="add">[enclosed]</char> the Carmeli <char style="add">[garden-land]</char>, Pa’arai <char style="add">[gaping]</char> the Arbi <char style="add">[an ambush]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />Yig’al <char style="add">[He Redeems]</char> the son of Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char> of Tzovah <char style="add">[station]</char>, Bani <char style="add">[built]</char> the Gadi <char style="add">[my fortune]</char> [an invader: a troop: fortune],</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />Tzelek <char style="add">[fissure]</char> the ‘Amoni <char style="add">[tribal]</char>, Nachrai <char style="add">[snorter]</char> the Be’erot <char style="add">[wells]</char>, armourbearer to Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> the son of Tz’ruyah <char style="add">[balsam]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />‘Ira <char style="add">[watchful of a city]</char> an Yitri <char style="add">[a remnant: excellence]</char>, Garev <char style="add">[scabby]</char> an Yitri <char style="add">[a remnant: excellence]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my light (flame)]</char> the Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char>: thirty and seven in all.</para>
  <chapter number="24" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And again the anger of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was kindled against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and he moved David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> against them to say, Go, number Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />For the king said to Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> the captain of the host, which <char style="add">[was]</char> with him, Go now through all the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, from Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char> even to Be’er-sheva <char style="add">[Well of the sevenfold Oath]</char>, and number you<char style="ord">2f</char> the people, that I may know the number of the people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> said unto the king, Now the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> add unto the people, how many soever they be, an hundredfold, and that the eyes of my lord the king may see <char style="add">[it]</char>: but why does my lord the king delight in this thing?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Yet the king’s word prevailed against Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, and against the captains of the host. And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> and the captains of the host went out from the presence of the king, to number the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And they passed over Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>, and pitched in ‘Aeo’er <char style="add">[Ruins]</char>, on the right side of the city that <char style="add">[lies]</char> in the midst of the river of Gad <char style="add">[Good Fortune with Troublesome Effort]</char>, and toward Ya’zer <char style="add">[Helped]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Then they came to Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>, and to the land of Tachtim-Hodshi <char style="add">[lowest-moon]</char>; and they came to Dan-Ya’an <char style="add">[purposeful judgment]</char>, and about to Tzidon <char style="add">[Hunting]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And came to the strong hold of Tzor <char style="add">[a rock]</char>, and to all the cities of the Hivi <char style="add">[Villagers]</char>, and of the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchants]</char>: and they went out to the south of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, <char style="add">[even]</char> to Be’er-sheva <char style="add">[Well of the sevenfold Oath]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />So when they had gone through all the land, they came to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> at the end of nine months and twenty days.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> gave up the sum of the number of the people unto the king: and there were in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> eight hundred thousand valiant men that drew the sword; and the men of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised] [were]</char> five hundred thousand men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s heart struck him after that he had numbered the people. And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, I have sinned greatly in that I have done: and now, I beseech <char style="pn">(to call upon; appeal; beg)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, take away the iniquity of you<char style="ord">i</char> servant; for I have done very foolishly.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />For when David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> was up in the morning, the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto the prophet Gad <char style="add">[Good Fortune with Troublesome Effort]</char>, David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s seer, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Go and say unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, I offer you<char style="ord">i</char> three <char style="add">[things]</char>; choose you<char style="ord">i</char> one of them, that I may <char style="add">[do it]</char> unto you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />So Gad <char style="add">[Good Fortune with Troublesome Effort]</char> came to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and told him, and said unto him, Shall seven years of famine come unto you<char style="ord">i</char> in your<char style="ord">i</char> land? or will you<char style="ord">i</char> flee three months before your<char style="ord">i</char> enemies, while they pursue you<char style="ord">i</char>? or that there be three days’ pestilence in your<char style="ord">i</char> land? now advise, and see what answer I shall return to him that sent me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said unto Gad <char style="add">[Good Fortune with Troublesome Effort]</char>, I am in a great strait: let us fall now into the hand of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; for his mercies <char style="add">[are]</char> great: and let me not fall into the hand of man.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />So the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> sent a pestilence upon Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> from the morning even to the time appointed: and there died of the people from Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char> even to Be’er-sheva <char style="add">[Well of the sevenfold Oath]</char> seventy thousand men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And when the angel stretched out his hand upon Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> to destroy it, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> repented him of the evil, and said to the angel that destroyed the people, It is enough: stay now your<char style="ord">i</char> hand. And the angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was by the threshing place of Aravnah <char style="add">[I shall shout for joy]</char> the Y’vusi <char style="add">[Threshers]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> spoke unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> when he saw the angel that struck the people, and said, Lo, I have sinned, and I have done wickedly: but these sheep, what have they done? let your<char style="ord">i</char> hand, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, be against me, and against my father’s house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And Gad <char style="add">[Good Fortune with Troublesome Effort]</char> came that day to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and said unto him, Go up, rear an altar unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in the threshing floor of Aravnah <char style="add">[I shall shout for joy]</char> the Y’vusi <char style="add">[Threshers]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, according to the saying of Gad <char style="add">[Good Fortune with Troublesome Effort]</char>, went up as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And Aravnah <char style="add">[I shall shout for joy]</char> looked, and saw the king and his servants coming on toward him: and Aravnah <char style="add">[I shall shout for joy]</char> went out, and bowed himself before the king on his face upon the ground.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Aravnah <char style="add">[I shall shout for joy]</char> said, For what reason is my lord the king come to his servant? And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said, To buy the threshing floor of you<char style="ord">i</char>, to build an altar unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, that the plague may be detained <char style="pn">(held)</char> from the people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And Aravnah <char style="add">[I shall shout for joy]</char> said unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, Let my lord the king take and offer up what <char style="add">[seems]</char> good unto him: behold, <char style="add">[here be]</char> oxen for burnt sacrifice, and threshing instruments and <char style="add">[other]</char> instruments of the oxen for wood.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />All these <char style="add">[things]</char> did Aravnah <char style="add">[I shall shout for joy]</char>, <char style="add">[as]</char> a king, give unto the king. And Aravnah <char style="add">[I shall shout for joy]</char> said unto the king, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> accept you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And the king said unto Aravnah <char style="add">[I shall shout for joy]</char>, No; but I will surely buy <char style="add">[it]</char> of you<char style="ord">i</char> at a price: neither will I offer burnt offerings unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of that which does cost me nothing. So David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> bought the threshing floor and the oxen for fifty shekels of silver.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> built there an altar unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and offered burnt offerings and peace offerings. So the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was entreated for the land, and the plague was detained <char style="pn">(held)</char> from Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
</usx>